{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms","id":1289923,"title":"Mortal Kombat! (Wombat) Wherein Prototype00 thinks about Lunar Animal Forms.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-20T07:54:56-08:00","id":1289923,"title":"Mortal Kombat! (Wombat) Wherein Prototype00 thinks about Lunar Animal Forms.","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Foul Anathema, you shall tempt the souls of men, NO LONGER!</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>*meow*</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>There is no dissuading me, I have chased you across THREE DIRECTIONS!</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>*purrrrr*</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>CEASE YOUR BLANDISHMENTS, TEMPTRESS!</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Hiss!*</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Yes, this can only end in death, make peace with your foul deity, Frenzied Moon Mad!</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Later, Anja would ponder the briefness of existence as she surveyed the wailing crowd of Shikari, Realm veterans and shocked Dynasts that gathered in the cul-de-sac. She licked the blood off her paws and padded off, just another unseen stray...</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So animal forms, get the biggest and baddest and go all Kaiju Combat, right?! Wreck absolutely everything as a Tyrant Lizard!<br /> <br /> Well not quite.<br /> <br /> 1. Kaiju combat is mote expensive, and will immediately (most times) make you go iconic, which is real bad.<br /> <br /> 2. Well what about the rad attacks? So many dice of damage! Well, I'm not 100% sure you can use an animal's damage but not their dice pool to hit. And animal accuracy is absolute cow pucky. Its real bad. Most times you will be more accurate in your human form than if you are attacking as a Pestletail.<br /> <br /> So what to do? I think the name of the game is <b>Mote Efficiency</b>. Getting the most for your 4 mote shapechange commitment.<br /> <br /> Take the humble Housecat, for example. Not very impressive, is it, what with it's poor accuracy and crap damage. Why would I choose that?<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think the Cat is one of the deadliest forms you can take out of the core animal choices. Let me tell you why.<br /> <br /> 1. These items are important: Re: Lunar Shapeshifting<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">She<u><i><b> may</b></i></u> use the animal\u2019s natural weapons, including their listed dice pool and damage value. (Note that she uses the same pool for withering and decisive attacks). Any dice over her own base (Dexterity + Brawl) count as Charm dice, but damage doesn\u2019t count against the amount she may add with the Strength Excellency. If her (Dexterity + Brawl) pool is higher than the attack pool for a natural weapon, her withering attacks with it gain +1 Accuracy.<br /> <br /> She gains the animal\u2019s innate special abilities and Merits. Dice or successes added by these count as Charm bonuses.<br /> <br /> She may unlock an animal shape\u2019s mundane latent abilities (but not magical abilities) for six experience points or three bonus points each. Once she\u2019s unlocked a latent ability for one form, it\u2019s unlocked for all forms capable of using it. She doesn\u2019t need to unlock latent abilities to use the distract, disarm, and unhorse gambits in animal forms.</div>2 Cats have:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Ambush Hunter: The cat adds three dice on all attack rolls made from stealth.<br /> <br /> Underfoot Menace (Latent): The cat treats any attack it<br /> makes against a larger enemy as being made from stealth<br /> for the purposes of its Ambush Hunter and Stalking<br /> Shadow Hunter special attacks.<br /> <br /> Tiny Creature: Cats add +2 Evasion against any attack<br /> made by a larger foe. In addition, larger characters subtract<br /> two successes from any Awareness-based roll made<br /> to notice it.</div>Now do you see where I am going with this? No? Let's put up an example then, Anja works well.<br /> <br /> Lets say Anja has 5 Strength, 5 Dex and 3 Stamina (the stamina isn't important, I just put it in to demonstrate that you can still have a good value if you max Strength and Dex.)<br /> <br /> In cat form, she doesn't have to use the cat's attack, she can use her own unarmed attack, say, a light weapon every creature possesses.<br /> <br /> But her unarmed attack benefits from cat related special talents, especially the ones I mentioned above.<br /> <br /> 1. For her attack stat, let's say she has (Dex 5 + Brawl 5) to attack, so 10 base dice, 11 with a specialty (cat-fu, say). She adds 4 for using a light weapon (unarmed) so 15, and stunts for 2 more 17. So far, so normal, most martial artists have as good a pool.<br /> <br /> Now she tacks on Ambush Hunter, and all of a sudden, unless she is fighting Mice of the Sun, she is rolling 20 dice with absolutely no motes spent. She still hits for 12 + threshold success damage (with 5 Str), and if she wants to keep her mote expenditure below anima flaring (i.e. 4 motes) she can roll 24 dice to attack.<br /> <br /> As a cat. A common, back-alley stray.<br /> <br /> And not only that<br /> <br /> 2. For her defence, lets say she splurged and has (Dex 5 + Dodge 5), 11 with a specialty. So thats a base Dodge DV of 6. She stunts it for a Dodge DV of 7. Thats pretty good, really. Quite hard to hi...<br /> <br /> Because she's a cat and for no other reason, her dodge DV is now 9. Even with 20 dice, you are hard pressed to hit. And she hasn't even spent any motes yet. And she can hit like a master assassin.<br /> <br /> TLDR: Biggest Beast is not best beast. You want mote efficency? Cat-punch things to death, highest accuracy and DV boost for 4 mote commitment.<br /> <br /> Did I get that wrong, am I dreaming, please do tell me. In the meantime, I'll keep combing for unexpected gems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-20-2019, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:39:23-08:00","id":1289944,"title":"","content":"A lot of that, yeah, you're right. Big forms are quite expensive. Though I'd argue there's mote efficiency in getting that bigger dice pool, at least if you're attacking with a high damage weapon (it's not worth it if you're using a low damage weapon).<br /> <br /> But, without fists, I'm not sure you actually can use your own Unarmed attack. It's a good point, and I think I'll ask it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:03:58-08:00","id":1289957,"title":"","content":"For other good shapes maybe Clawstrider or Dog? Pack Hunting is very good if you have the latent upgrade and also several human allies (or if you just have several same species allies). Clawstriders get a 15-damage attack, and ambush hunter for even more accuracy (though nothing like underfoot menace). Dogs get some nice defend other effects.<br /> <br /> On the less attack-oriented side, you can get some very high soaks without having to wear armor, admittedly many are legendary size. Impenetrable Armor (-1 overwhelming) goes well with this, especially against people without artifact weapons. Also, I am amused by the image of an evasion 6 pestletail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:14:43-08:00","id":1289962,"title":"","content":"I think we all know the ultimate hit-and-run form is... the giant stick insect!<br /> Hide with Camouflage, attack with Ambush Hunter, and flurry a disengage... which auto-suceeds!<br /> You can always grow your leg back later.<br /> <br /> (On a more serious note, if you have lots of Ox-Bodies go with Bear. Berzerker is very useful.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:10:30-08:00","id":1290018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms#post1289923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Kaiju combat is mote expensive, and will immediately (most times) make you go iconic, which is real bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does this come from? Maybe I missed a Charm or two on the matter but I'm not sure why it's mote expensive? Cite/link? (I am a KS backer so have access to backer-only stuff if it's in there).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms#post1289923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Well what about the rad attacks? So many dice of damage! Well, I'm not 100% sure you can use an animal's damage but not their dice pool to hit.<br /> <br /> And animal accuracy is absolute cow pucky. Its real bad. Most times you will be more accurate in your human form than if you are attacking as a Pestletail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that is a specific example and probably one of the worst tbh. Yeah the pestletail's dice pool sucks, but others are better. Tyrant lizard is biting at 11, which is basically maxed Attribute + Ability + Specialty with a heavy mortal weapon, 1 less than an Artifact heavy weapon accuracy, but the slam is 12, so the same as an Artifact heavy weapon for to-hit. Talons are 13 dice, so falling between Artifact medium and heavy melee weapons to hit. Though all of these have fewer raw damage dice than comparable-accuracy Artifact weapon withering damage stats assuming maxed Strength like your Anja.<br /> <br /> This is also before considering some of the special attack and merit benefits, though those benefits in an animal form have to be weighed against the likelihood of comparable or better Evocations if you're using an Artifact in human form.<br /> <br /> Looking through - Armored Terrors, bears, claw striders, great cats, and quoll-lions also all have at least decent &quot;weapon&quot; stats, though &quot;decent&quot; is certainly contextual.<br /> <br /> At the same time, probably the best user for some of these higher power animal forms is frankly <i>not</i> your Str 5/Dex 5/Brawl 5/Dodge 5 optimized warrior, but someone with much less investment in physical attributes, to whom 11-13 dice and 14-16 damage dice are a big upgrade to what they might be able to throw around in human form<br /> <br /> Is this disappointing? Maybe, idk, it depends on what role you think shapeshifting should play and your personal expectations. I am not sure there is a way to make a given animal-form with a given set of stats/dice pools mutually appealing to both the combat-optimized 5/5/3 berserker and the physical-tertiary sorcerer who didn't even favor a physical attribute at all.<br /> <br /> The alternative is scaling stats meaning instead of assuming a given stat block you just get +s and -s to different stats on top of your base stats as applicable (like things work with the different forms in Werewolf), which is both more complicated, and IIRC just more ripe for &quot;abuse&quot; (such as it is) when layered on top of the high end combat-character's high-end physical stats getting pumped even higher (see also: 2e DBT's stat increases).<br /> <br /> As I flip through the animal forms in the Core it is obvious that the dice pools are balanced against essentially the concept of &quot;how would this animal do if attacking a normal human,&quot; which makes sense since most people in Creation are normal humans even if probably 99% of PCs in Exalted are, well, Exalted. The stats are designed around &quot;what makes sense in an in-setting context&quot; not &quot;what provides a particular challenge vs an Exalt&quot;; most Exalts are not going to be worried about a pestle tail hitting them unless they have some significant penalties stacked up, whereas mortals should rightly be concerned being around these things.<br /> <br /> And as we all know, &quot;what makes sense in an in-setting context&quot; not &quot;what provides a particular challenge vs an Exalt&quot; is a very different kind of antagonist design mentality than say D&amp;D's, for both good and ill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-20-2019, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:40:10-08:00","id":1290032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms#post1289923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TLDR: Biggest Beast is not best beast. You want mote efficency? Cat-punch things to death, highest accuracy and DV boost for 4 mote commitment.<br /> <br /> Did I get that wrong, am I dreaming, please do tell me. In the meantime, I'll keep combing for unexpected gems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XfeFVSpGiWY\" data-code=\"XfeFVSpGiWY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XfeFVSpGiWY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:54:07-08:00","id":1290043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290018#post1290018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does this come from? Maybe I missed a Charm or two on the matter but I'm not sure why it's mote expensive? Cite/link? (I am a KS backer so have access to backer-only stuff if it's in there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Towering Beast Form isn't in the stuff previewed in the Kickstarter, but a few months ago a playtester wrote a thread revealing some stuff.<br /> <br /> One thing they said was that taking the form of something with Legendary Size took not 4m, like most forms, but 15 motes... and you have to spend 4m a round in combat, or 4m an hour outside combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:35:30-08:00","id":1290055,"title":"","content":"I don't think I interpreted this (quoted) as allowing you to use your unarmed attack's Accuracy on Withering attacks. (If Anja <i>was </i>using her unarmed profile and Strength to attack, would an animal form's talons and fangs have the Bashing tag?) It seems as though animals use the same pool for withering and decisive, with an optional +1 Accuracy to Withering if your Dex/Brawl exceeds the animal's dice pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She may use the animal\u2019s natural weapons, including their listed dice pool and damage value. (Note that she uses the same pool for withering and decisive attacks). Any dice over her own base (Dexterity + Brawl) count as Charm dice, but damage doesn\u2019t count against the amount she may add with the Strength Excellency. If her (Dexterity + Brawl) pool is higher than the attack pool for a natural weapon, her withering attacks with it gain +1 Accuracy. </div> </div> </div>If Dex + Brawl, here, does not include Accuracy, Anja is limited to a dice pool of 11+Attr+Attr (let's say 21 + stunt) because anything in excess of her Dex+Brawl would be Charm dice.<br /> <br /> If it does, as in your example, then Anja gets 5+5+1+4 (acc) + 1 (acc bonus for dex+brawl in excess of form's dice pool) + up to 10 Charm dice = 26 + stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:54:04-08:00","id":1290062,"title":"","content":"Commoner slaying house cats are back baby! Now let's take out a party of low-level adventurers.<br /> <br /> I think you are onto something here, for the most part, I suspect that such a small creature - while good on the offense is going to be very vulnerable to large clinches and other potential gambits, like trampling. You have your dex charms to keep you safe for a while, and the strength helps a lot as well though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","user":"Nabirius","date":". 02-20-2019, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:40:52-08:00","id":1290101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1289944#post1289944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of that, yeah, you're right. Big forms are quite expensive. Though I'd argue there's mote efficiency in getting that bigger dice pool, at least if you're attacking with a high damage weapon (it's not worth it if you're using a low damage weapon).<br /> <br /> But, without fists, I'm not sure you actually can use your own Unarmed attack. It's a good point, and I think I'll ask it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you need Fists to unarmed attack in Exalted because, I'm not 100%, but isn't the unarmed mortal weapon just describing brawling without a weapon? But indeed, a good question to ask the Devs (and if you don't, I will)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For other good shapes maybe Clawstrider or Dog? Pack Hunting is very good if you have the latent upgrade and also several human allies (or if you just have several same species allies). Clawstriders get a 15-damage attack, and ambush hunter for even more accuracy (though nothing like underfoot menace). Dogs get some nice defend other effects.<br /> <br /> On the less attack-oriented side, you can get some very high soaks without having to wear armor, admittedly many are legendary size. Impenetrable Armor (-1 overwhelming) goes well with this, especially against people without artifact weapons. Also, I am amused by the image of an evasion 6 pestletail. </div> </div> </div>The soak is the best thing about the large sized creatures in my opinion. There are reflexive charms that let you shapeshift in response to attacks, so they have their uses. Dogs and eagles were actually the next couple I was eyeing thanks to the special attacks and merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mean that is a specific example and probably one of the worst tbh. Yeah the pestletail's dice pool sucks, but others are better. Tyrant lizard is biting at 11, which is basically maxed Attribute + Ability + Specialty with a heavy mortal weapon, 1 less than an Artifact heavy weapon accuracy, but the slam is 12, so the same as an Artifact heavy weapon for to-hit. Talons are 13 dice, so falling between Artifact medium and heavy melee weapons to hit. Though all of these have fewer raw damage dice than comparable-accuracy Artifact weapon withering damage stats assuming maxed Strength like your Anja. </div> </div> </div>Their Dice pool are better, but not... y'know 20 dice pool hurled round with no mote expenditure. I know I did hyper focus on accuracy here, but when I look at the cost of going T-Rex an the fact that the housecat can absolutely murder given a character with good attributes (so it's good for a combat focused Lunar, even) I thought I'd point it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think I interpreted this (quoted) as allowing you to use your unarmed attack's Accuracy on Withering attacks. (If Anja <i>was </i>using her unarmed profile and Strength to attack, would an animal form's talons and fangs have the Bashing tag?) It seems as though animals use the same pool for withering and decisive, with an optional +1 Accuracy to Withering if your Dex/Brawl exceeds the animal's dice pool.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>See, the thing I'm doing here is I'm not even using the animal's attack at all. I thought about the difficulty of making the cat's attacks work for me (they have poor accuracy, damage is decent if you can get the accuracy up) and decided to use my own Unarmed attack pool which I am calculating in the usual fashion. Nothing in the rules that I have seen so far says that tiny creatures (miniscule probably has some rules about this) do less damage with their Unarmed attack pool compared to full sized creatures? So I am calculating the unarmed attack from scratch.<br /> <br /> The important word here in the description is &quot;May&quot; which I highlighted in the original post. You may use their attacks. But my post was that if you had other attack pools that you could reconstitute (like unarmed brawl for example) you could also use that, which turns out in the case of the Housecat to be a mote-efficient unhittable blender.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you are onto something here, for the most part, I suspect that such a small creature - while good on the offense is going to be very vulnerable to large clinches and other potential gambits, like trampling. You have your dex charms to keep you safe for a while, and the strength helps a lot as well though. </div> </div> </div>I agree (they are going to be smaller whenever that applies), but they still have to hit to grapple, which isn't trivial. Also, hilariously, housecat can probably wear Moonsilver armor. You aren't using martial arts or anything, wear the best Moonsilver light armor you can afford with bp!<br /> <br /> Edit: ARRRGH! I was referencing Anya Silverclaws (who is a cat totem Lunar in the lore) when I made the example, but I spelled her name wrong! Frack it, it's okay. Anja it is then. You're my first bootleg, obviously stolen, Drizzt style, character, hooray!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-20-2019, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:55:08-08:00","id":1290105,"title":"","content":"Anja also &quot;may&quot; attempt any Feat of Strength the form is capable of, which - by this interpretation of &quot;may&quot; - would mean that the subsequent provisions about the limits of the form's Strength are irrelevant, as she can opt to instead use her own Strength &quot;from scratch&quot;, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:59:58-08:00","id":1290108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290105#post1290105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anja also &quot;may&quot; attempt any Feat of Strength the form is capable of, which - by this interpretation of &quot;may&quot; - would mean that the subsequent provisions about the limits of the form's Strength are irrelevant, as she can opt to instead use her own Strength &quot;from scratch&quot;, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She may attempt any feat of strength that the animal is capable of performing. If the animal\u2019s effective Strength rating is lower than her own, she\u2019s limited to the lower value. If the form doesn\u2019t list a Strength rating for the purpose of feats, it\u2019s assumed to have Strength 1. </div> </div> </div>I think this specific rule covers Feats of Strength. For everything else:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she takes an action the animal has a listed dice pool for, she may use its dice pool. Any dice over her own base (Attribute + Ability) pool count as Charm dice and are subject to her dice cap (p. XX), potentially preventing her from using a form\u2019s full dice pool. If the animal\u2019s pool is lower than hers, or it has no listed pool, she may use her own dice pool, although the Storyteller may assess penalties if her shape is ill-suited to that action. </div> </div> </div>Edit: Checked with Vance, apparently completely legit<br /> :<br /> When a Lunar is Shapeshifted into a form of an animal, do they <i><b>have </b></i>to use the listed attacks in the animal's QC block? (The text says &quot;may use&quot;) Would it be possible to use their own human brawl pool and attack with the unarmed stats? (I.e. Dex + Brawl) but use the animal's special qualities?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1290107#post1290107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can use their own pools if they're higher. The only exception is Strength rating to qualify for feats of strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-20-2019, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:11:46-08:00","id":1290114,"title":"","content":"You don't spell combat with a k without creating certain expectations! I was expecting D'vorah as a bee totem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:16:12-08:00","id":1290116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290114#post1290114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't spell combat with a k without creating certain expectations! I was expecting D'vorah as a bee totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a certain segment of people, I don't think it's possible to spell that word pairing with a C anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:32:50-08:00","id":1290122,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure we\u2019ve only had an Anja Silverclaws in the lore ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:16:31-08:00","id":1290131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290122#post1290122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure we\u2019ve only had an Anja Silverclaws in the lore ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah? Phew! It was someone else misremembering then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:24:34-08:00","id":1290145,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s like Christmas and Calibration rolled into one!<br /> <br /> Vance just said you can use your own dice pool and the animal\u2019s Damage (or you have to...?) this is great for housecats!<br /> <br /> Kitties have a 12 Damage bite (as much as mortal martial arts masters who benchpress horses), that only applies to smaller things, except when attacking from stealth. Best part, it\u2019s entirely Str independent, so you can do basically stupid damage and dump (or don\u2019t focus on) strength!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:38:11-08:00","id":1290147,"title":"","content":"If I\u2019m reading his reply correctly, you have to use the animal\u2019s attack pool and the animal\u2019s damage pool. You get +1 accuracy if yours is bigger, but you can\u2019t just use your own Unarmed Attack instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:40:46-08:00","id":1290148,"title":"","content":"I'm... confused, because Vance said<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1290138#post1290138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have to use the natural weapon's pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which seems like it directly contradicts him saying &quot;they can use their own pools if they're higher&quot;. Am I missing things?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:41:22-08:00","id":1290150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290147#post1290147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I\u2019m reading his reply correctly, you have to use the animal\u2019s attack pool and the animal\u2019s damage pool. You get +1 accuracy if yours is bigger, but you can\u2019t just use your own Unarmed Attack instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>From previous replies:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can use their own pools if they're higher. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:46:35-08:00","id":1290154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290148#post1290148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... confused, because Vance said<br /> <br /> Which seems like it directly contradicts him saying &quot;they can use their own pools if they're higher&quot;. Am I missing things?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think where the confusion here is that \u201cpool\u201d can be used for 2 values. The first is Attack (Dex + Brawl) and the second is Damage (wtf ever animals use to calculate it, for Exalts it\u2019s Str + Weapon bonus)<br /> <br /> The Attack pool can be replaced with the Lunar\u2019s own form Dex + Brawl. The Damage pool cannot just be replaced by your Unarmed Damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:53:11-08:00","id":1290158,"title":"","content":"Vance was asked to distinguish between these:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>can they use the weapon stats of a normal unarmed strike? That is, can they attack with dex+brawl+4 to hit, strength+7 damage, or must they use one of the animal's natural weapons for dex+brawl+1 to hit?</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> And said to use the &quot;natural weapon&quot; pool - which in this pairing should be the second, your Dex + Brawl (+1, if your Dex+Brawl is better than the animal form's native dice pool.)<br /> <br /> You're still using your traits if they're better, but animal attacks don't benefit from Accuracy <i>except </i>for the listed possible +1 Acc in the rules paragraph, and you don't use the light weapon profile or damage calculation.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>As noted above, this &quot;merely&quot; limits Prototype's example case to 22 + stunt dice for accuracy, and a pool of 15 + stunt with no mote expenditure if you can use Ambush Hunter. With a potential of 12 damage per hit if you have the cat's other latent ability, + up to 5 from Excellencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 02-20-2019, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:53:51-08:00","id":1290159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290154#post1290154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think where the confusion here is that \u201cpool\u201d can be used for 2 values. The first is Attack (Dex + Brawl) and the second is Damage (wtf ever animals use to calculate it, for Exalts it\u2019s Str + Weapon bonus)<br /> <br /> The Attack pool can be replaced with the Lunar\u2019s own form Dex + Brawl. The Damage pool cannot just be replaced by your Unarmed Damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the post he's replying to and what he says, that doesn't appear to be what's being said?<br /> He says &quot;have to use the natural weapon's pool&quot; and &quot;have to use the animal's damage line&quot;, the former in response to a question touching on the attack dicepool, and it wouldn't make sense for the first line to be referring to the damage dicepool if the second one is as well.<br /> We may just have to ask him to hella spell it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:00:12-08:00","id":1290162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290158#post1290158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance was asked to distinguish between these:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;<b>can they use the weapon stats of a normal unarmed strike? That is, can they attack with dex+brawl+4 to hit, strength+7 damage, or must they use one of the animal's natural weapons for dex+brawl+1 to hit?</b>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And said to use the &amp;quot;natural weapon&amp;quot; pool - which in this pairing should be the second, your Dex + Brawl (+1, if your Dex+Brawl is better than the animal form's native dice pool.)<br /> <br /> You're still using your traits if they're better, but animal attacks don't benefit from Accuracy <i>except </i>for the listed possible +1 Acc in the rules paragraph, and you don't use the light weapon profile or damage calculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah is that so, well that means kitties are merely on par with Martial Arts Masters with their attack and damage. <br /> <br /> Ah, well. Need to double confirm with him if animals are forbidden to use Unarmed Strike (as still a bit unclear).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:50:31-08:00","id":1290189,"title":"","content":"So far my opinion on animal form combat (they are useful for so much more) is that it probably won\u2019t be as valuable to the fighty fighty murder Lunars baring more charms yet to be releveled. I actually find them more interesting for characters where fighting is a secondary to tertiary ordeal. Let\u2019s say you are a secondary fighter (Brawl 3) and only with average Dex (2) that means your pool is 5 +2 from excellency and assuming you stunt right another +5 from stunts for a total pool of 12. Considering a one point stunt is very easy you should always have a pool of 12 to attack then which would normally cost you 7 motes each turn, but in animal form is free with the minor cost of committing 4 motes. The goal then is to find an animal with a accuracy pool of 12+ with decent damage and defenses. You then have more motes to fuel more charms to either help in combat, excellency up a spell, or something else in the heat of battle (including running for your life). Great Cats would be a good choice for my example with a claw attack of 13 dice and 12 damage<br /> <br /> Basically for me animals seem to be a great way to conserve motes so you can fuel other powers in combat.<br /> <br /> However most animals don\u2019t have the accuracy dice to really save motes if you are they type that has 5 dex + 5 brawl +10 excellency dice since most of the animals that even begin to near that large of a dice pool. They can save some motes but you might be better off with a cool set of evocations &amp; martial arts. <br /> <br /> Mind you this could all change depending on what charms are to come but at this point this is my opinion for what it matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:53:10-08:00","id":1290191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290159#post1290159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the post he's replying to and what he says, that doesn't appear to be what's being said?<br /> He says &quot;have to use the natural weapon's pool&quot; and &quot;have to use the animal's damage line&quot;, the former in response to a question touching on the attack dicepool, and it wouldn't make sense for the first line to be referring to the damage dicepool if the second one is as well.<br /> We may just have to ask him to hella spell it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you seeing these replies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:58:50-08:00","id":1290192,"title":"","content":"This does look to be the direction the shapeshifting rules push you to go.<br /> <br /> Don't go looking for forms that express what your character is. Rather look for forms that provide merits that potentially equate to no charm bonus die and look for base dice pools that provide the biggest bang for buck in terms of free excellency.<br /> <br /> This leaves animals balanced in the middle of the road less desirable and options at extremes like housecats or pestletail king of the pack, or should I say clowder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:06:19-08:00","id":1290199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290192#post1290192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does look to be the direction the shapeshifting rules push you to go.<br /> <br /> Don't go looking for forms that express what your character is. Rather look for forms that provide merits that potentially equate to no charm bonus die and look for base dice pools that provide the biggest bang for buck in terms of free excellency.<br /> <br /> This leaves animals balanced in the middle of the road less desirable and options at extremes like housecats or pestletail king of the pack, or should I say clowder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? Sometimes it is just fun to play with the combat engine. Even if it is inefficient I still want to be a rampaging tyrant lizard** damn the exorbitant mote cost! Because this is EXALTED and the rule of cool shall reign!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">**Actually I want to play a rhino beetle swords man or a orchid mantis assassin. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-20-2019, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:26:44-08:00","id":1290207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290192#post1290192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does look to be the direction the shapeshifting rules push you to go.<br /> <br /> Don't go looking for forms that express what your character is. Rather look for forms that provide merits that potentially equate to no charm bonus die and look for base dice pools that provide the biggest bang for buck in terms of free excellency.<br /> <br /> This leaves animals balanced in the middle of the road less desirable and options at extremes like housecats or pestletail king of the pack, or should I say clowder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, ah well there goes my dream of Brawler kitteh. Small Cats are \u201cmerely\u201d the most more efficient accurate animal shape (ie they match the dice pools of attack and damage of Master Martial Artists). *sigh*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:29:25-08:00","id":1290208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290147#post1290147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I\u2019m reading his reply correctly, you have to use the animal\u2019s attack pool and the animal\u2019s damage pool. You get +1 accuracy if yours is bigger, but you can\u2019t just use your own Unarmed Attack instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed that this just meant that people who weren't minmaxed for combat could still take advantage of animal forms even if they didn't have the stats but that you can't just be a household cat and do 20 L to an enemy without charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:42:39-08:00","id":1290213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290191#post1290191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you seeing these replies?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ask the Devs thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page1058\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-devs/page1058</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:46:34-08:00","id":1290216,"title":"","content":"In general, it seems like strength and stamina aren't great investments for the animal-form-combatant, since you can't use them for attack/damage. They still affect excellency (thought stunting can give you a decent cap anyways), and probably have good charms.<br /> <br /> Looking through corebook animals for things with good all-around stats and not legendary size, hoping for forms useable by someone without much investment in combat:<br /> <br /> Bear (12 die attack at 11 damage, parry 3, soak 10), claw strider (12 die attack at 11 damage, evasion 4, soak 7), eagle (10 die attack at 11 damage, evasion 4, soak 2, flight), Gorilla (10 die attack at 13, parry 4, soak 6), Great Cat (13 die attack at 12 damage, evasion and parry 4, soak 6), or Quoll-Lion (11 die attack at 10 damage, evasion 4, soak 5).<br /> <br /> The biggest weakness here might be defense more than attack - Most of these have 10-13 die attack pulls and some way to get more from merits, but only 3-4 defense with few merit boosts.<br /> Turning into an animal might be the good option for a primarily ranged fighter - you want a good dex for ranged attacks, and a good dodge for defending at range, so if you get stuck in close range you can rely on your animal form for attacks while using your own Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T21:43:49-08:00","id":1290235,"title":"","content":"So just a final 3 point After Action Report of Death Kitty:<br /> <br /> 1. You can get very respectable Attack and Damage with just a Dex investment, on par with an unarmed martial arts master, no strength needed.(Cats probably are the only critters that match the Accuracy buff of light weapons)<br /> <br /> 2. You probably still come out ahead of your mote commitment due to the persistent 2 Evasion bonus<br /> <br /> 3. I mean it\u2019s a Cat that can probably Bruce Lee experienced Dynasts to death, what more do you want?<br /> <br /> In unrelated news, I\u2019m beat. I should stop hyping up my discoveries and then getting deflated. -_-<br /> <br /> Edit: I should also add that you have an innate ability in this form that EATS SUCCESSES from rolls to perceive you, also making it a fantastic infiltration tool that you can fight full power in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-22-2019, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T22:46:27-08:00","id":1290245,"title":"","content":"AutXautY, I kind of agree with you about Str and Sta, but I imagine Towering Beast Form will require one of those at 4 or 5.<br /> There's also damage and soak charms, that aren't capped the way attack pools are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T19:56:37-08:00","id":1290638,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion: death kitty is a very bad outcome of the rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T20:44:22-08:00","id":1290645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290638#post1290638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion: death kitty is a very bad outcome of the rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sad face* How so? I mean I was massively amused at my mental imgage of the killer housecat. What goes wrong if you have Invincible Sword Princess fighting evenly with Sasha the Alleyway Queen?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or did you mean that it was a sub-optimal outcome, in which case, Firewands at Dawn, Good Sir/Ma\u2019am/Citizen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-22-2019, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T00:15:48-08:00","id":1290672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290216#post1290216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, it seems like strength and stamina aren't great investments for the animal-form-combatant, since you can't use them for attack/damage. They still affect excellency (thought stunting can give you a decent cap anyways), and probably have good charms.<br /> <br /> Looking through corebook animals for things with good all-around stats and not legendary size, hoping for forms useable by someone without much investment in combat:<br /> <br /> Bear (12 die attack at 11 damage, parry 3, soak 10), claw strider (12 die attack at 11 damage, evasion 4, soak 7), eagle (10 die attack at 11 damage, evasion 4, soak 2, flight), Gorilla (10 die attack at 13, parry 4, soak 6), Great Cat (13 die attack at 12 damage, evasion and parry 4, soak 6), or Quoll-Lion (11 die attack at 10 damage, evasion 4, soak 5).<br /> <br /> The biggest weakness here might be defense more than attack - Most of these have 10-13 die attack pulls and some way to get more from merits, but only 3-4 defense with few merit boosts.<br /> Turning into an animal might be the good option for a primarily ranged fighter - you want a good dex for ranged attacks, and a good dodge for defending at range, so if you get stuck in close range you can rely on your animal form for attacks while using your own Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I\u2019d reply to this too after some noodling. Stamina probably still helps as an animal, as you can use your own native soak (which might be higher than your form, see: Housecat), but Strength is completely useless, since you have to use animal damage, independent of Str.<br /> <br /> So based on my clearer understanding, with 5 Dex, 5 Brawl and both the latent talents, if you want to fight as anything other than a cat and you want better combat stats:<br /> <br /> Your Animal Form Accuracy has to be 14+ thanks to Ambush Hunter and Underfoot Menace (Latent)<br /> <br /> Your Animal Form Damage has to be 12+ thanks to Stalking Shadow Hunter (Latent) and Underfoot Menace (Latent) (a couple of non kaiju animals beat this, but not the accuracy)<br /> <br /> For safety, you\u2019d better have an animal form merit that adds +2 to your EV and eats 2+ successes from any attempts to notice you.<br /> <br /> Y\u2019see, the bummer about having 10+ but not 14+ Accuracy as an animal shape (lots of \u201ccombat shapes\u201d fall in this range) is that you can\u2019t apply the free +1 Accuracy bonus from having a higher pool in Human form than animal form (you can as a Housecat).<br /> <br /> Thus I submit the following contentious statement:<br /> <br /> If you have 5 Dex and are willing to take both the latent Cat talents, the cat probably beats out all the non-Kaiju forms for the combination of accuracy/damage and Mote Efficiency, with Eagle coming a close second for first round ambush shenanigans (then you can shift into a cat afterwards).<br /> <br /> If you are a no moon shaman and just want to maul something in a pinch, just pick one of the Combat shapes mentioned previously.<br /> <br /> All hail Death Kitty! <br /> <br /> Disclaimer: There is a high possibility that I am wrong or have missed something as this seems whimsically crazy even to me.<br /> <br /> Edit: If your animal is non Kaiju and has a... 15-16+ Damage Attack, you\u2019ve probably beaten the Cat in the attack/damage department (your Raw Damage is 4+ higher than a cat\u2019s, which means your Accuracy matters less)<br /> <br /> Nothing I\u2019ve seen so far beats the cat on defense (not considering soak) yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-22-2019, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:28:49-08:00","id":1290688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290638#post1290638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion: death kitty is a very bad outcome of the rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts as well, I am increasingly edgy about the mechanical wonkiness on Lunar shapeshifting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:38:04-08:00","id":1290691,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the &quot;wonky&quot; in this case is primarily the two latents that provide consistent passive +3 accuracy and +8 damage to the housecat.<br /> <br /> That's not really about how Lunars work and more about &quot;while it seems amusing to let a housecat have the damage rating of a Str 5 man with a machete, perhaps one should not have done this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:49:57-08:00","id":1290694,"title":"","content":"That's fair, it's not inherently Lunar shapeshifting that's the problem, just the way it, animal stats and abilities and the ability to use normal dicepools regardless of shape, sometimes in weird places (you can use native soak apparently? <i>Really?</i>) that is wonky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T02:58:59-08:00","id":1290702,"title":"","content":"Personally I think shapeshifting is the issue. There's not really a dignified way to lose a fight to an opponent with the Tiny Creature merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T05:36:57-08:00","id":1290725,"title":"","content":"Tyrant Mouse Dominion would seem to offer a path forward in terms of rules that should be applied more broadly.<br /> <br /> Also miniature tyrant lizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:07:17-08:00","id":1290764,"title":"","content":"Is this what it feel like to live long enough to become the villain? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My thoughts as well, I am increasingly edgy about the mechanical wonkiness on Lunar shapeshifting </div> </div> </div>I mean, if by wonky, you mean that there are quite simple rules in place that I and other forumites clarified to the Nth degree on the ask the Devs page? I mean, it isn't as simple as: Here is animal QC sheet, go nuts, but I ask, should it be? After all said animal is also a Silver demigod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be fair, the &quot;wonky&quot; in this case is primarily the two latents that provide consistent passive +3 accuracy and +8 damage to the housecat.<br /> <br /> That's not really about how Lunars work and more about &quot;while it seems amusing to let a housecat have the damage rating of a Str 5 man with a machete, perhaps one should not have done this.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I think shapeshifting is the issue. There's not really a dignified way to lose a fight to an opponent with the Tiny Creature merit. </div> </div> </div>Why do people not like the idea of a small, underestimated creature absolutely dominating combat I wonder? That is the key to some of the most dramatic/comedic/awesome scenes in media that I know today. Just remember Yoda taking on Dooku in the Attack of the Clones or Baby Groot in basically all his scenes?<br /> <br /> Is it just because it's silly and silly doesn't belong in Exalted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tyrant Mouse Dominion would seem to offer a path forward in terms of rules that should be applied more broadly. </div> </div> </div>Miniscule Creature is it's own size merit and has it's own rules (elucidated in said charm) and Tiny Creature is it's own merit and has it's own rules (elucidated in the Tiny Creature merit). I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;more broadly&quot;?<br /> <br /> In short, I am wondering why people have trouble with the image of a Housecat taking Exalted foes apart, especially if said Housecat is actually a Silver demigod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:08:02-08:00","id":1290766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290672#post1290672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought I\u2019d reply to this too after some noodling. Stamina probably still helps as an animal, as you can use your own native soak (which might be higher than your form, see: Housecat), but Strength is completely useless, since you have to use animal damage, independent of Str.<br /> <br /> So based on my clearer understanding, with 5 Dex, 5 Brawl and both the latent talents, if you want to fight as anything other than a cat and you want better combat stats:<br /> <br /> Your Animal Form Accuracy has to be 14+ thanks to Ambush Hunter and Underfoot Menace (Latent)<br /> <br /> Your Animal Form Damage has to be 12+ thanks to Stalking Shadow Hunter (Latent) and Underfoot Menace (Latent) (a couple of non kaiju animals beat this, but not the accuracy)<br /> <br /> For safety, you\u2019d better have an animal form merit that adds +2 to your EV and eats 2+ successes from any attempts to notice you.<br /> <br /> Y\u2019see, the bummer about having 10+ but not 14+ Accuracy as an animal shape (lots of \u201ccombat shapes\u201d fall in this range) is that you can\u2019t apply the free +1 Accuracy bonus from having a higher pool in Human form than animal form (you can as a Housecat).<br /> <br /> Thus I submit the following contentious statement:<br /> <br /> If you have 5 Dex and are willing to take both the latent Cat talents, the cat probably beats out all the non-Kaiju forms for the combination of accuracy/damage and Mote Efficiency, with Eagle coming a close second for first round ambush shenanigans (then you can shift into a cat afterwards).<br /> <br /> If you are a no moon shaman and just want to maul something in a pinch, just pick one of the Combat shapes mentioned previously.<br /> <br /> All hail Death Kitty!<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: There is a high possibility that I am wrong or have missed something as this seems whimsically crazy even to me.<br /> <br /> Edit: If your animal is non Kaiju and has a... 15-16+ Damage Attack, you\u2019ve probably beaten the Cat in the attack/damage department (your Raw Damage is 4+ higher than a cat\u2019s, which means your Accuracy matters less)<br /> <br /> Nothing I\u2019ve seen so far beats the cat on defense (not considering soak) yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I misread the rules on shapeshifting soak. Stamina is still useful for shapeshifters who turn into low-soak animals.<br /> <br /> Venomous snake can compete with cat on defense, but has no way to get good accuracy or withering damage. Poison gives a nice decisive though. Possibly worth using with Quicksilver Second Face just for a decisive attack?<br /> <br /> I would add clawstrider and pestetail to the list of optimal combat forms alongside cat, with claw strider being useful if you have allies in melee and pestetail focusing on soak+damage over accuracy.<br /> I agree that most of the straightforwardly good at fighting forms are good for lunars with little-to-no combat investment as an emergency option, but not for lunars with a good dex+brawl pool of their own.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to note that a cat's low soak can be mitigated with moonsilver armor (probably light to keep your evasion high). Just for the mental image of a cat in a suit of silver armor.<br /> <br /> A lot of animals have merits+special attacks interacting with grapples. I wonder if there's any pattern of shifting forms with Quicksilver Second Face to take advantage of a bunch of these.<br /> <br /> Edit: the best of these are on River Dragons and Tyrant Lizards, who are legendary size. Unless shapeshifting resets mauling bite, the best I found is be a Death Moa/Angler Lizard, grapple someone at short range, and then turn into a bear or great cat for mauling bite. Maybe there's some value to switching between River Dragon and Tyrant Lizard using Behemoth-and-Flea Mastery to use a death roll followed by a ferocious bite followed by a deadly thrash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 02-22-2019, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:30:48-08:00","id":1290779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290764#post1290764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this what it feel like to live long enough to become the villain? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, if by wonky, you mean that there are quite simple rules in place that I and other forumites clarified to the Nth degree on the ask the Devs page? I mean, it isn't as simple as: Here is animal QC sheet, go nuts, but I ask, should it be? After all said animal is also a Silver demigod.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why do people not like the idea of a small, underestimated creature absolutely dominating combat I wonder? That is the key to some of the most dramatic/comedic/awesome scenes in media that I know today. Just remember Yoda taking on Dooku in the Attack of the Clones or Baby Groot in basically all his scenes?<br /> <br /> Is it just because it's silly and silly doesn't belong in Exalted?<br /> <br /> <br /> Miniscule Creature is it's own size merit and has it's own rules (elucidated in said charm) and Tiny Creature is it's own merit and has it's own rules (elucidated in the Tiny Creature merit). I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;more broadly&quot;?<br /> <br /> In short, I am wondering why people have trouble with the image of a Housecat taking Exalted foes apart, especially if said Housecat is actually a Silver demigod?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean wonky as not sufficiently clear (i.e. they should not require repeated questions for clarification) and, for me, creating a significant, immersion breaking gulf between the rules and the flavour of the game.<br /> <br /> And your examples of awesome scenes are probably the scenes I liked least from both of those films.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think it's because it just <i>feels</i> wrong to me. Surprise turning into a bear for combat is awesome. Getting your butt kicked by a little girl because she's secretly a kung fu badass is cool. Getting slaughtered by a housecat because of some dice shenanigans based on pools from a completely different shape is... less awesome. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:00:15-08:00","id":1290790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290766#post1290766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason I misread the rules on shapeshifting soak. Stamina is still useful for shapeshifters who turn into low-soak animals.<br /> <br /> Venomous snake can compete with cat on defense, but has no way to get good accuracy or withering damage. Poison gives a nice decisive though. Possibly worth using with Quicksilver Second Face just for a decisive attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the ability to pick and choose shapes on the fly is a good reason to argue for the strength of the Pure-Shapeshift combatant. It is probably hell on the book-keeping though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would add clawstrider and pestetail to the list of optimal combat forms alongside cat, with claw strider being useful if you have allies in melee and pestetail focusing on soak+damage over accuracy.<br /> I agree that most of the straightforwardly good at fighting forms are good for lunars with little-to-no combat investment as an emergency option, but not for lunars with a good dex+brawl pool of their own. </div> </div> </div>You know, I have to say, mea-culpa, I shouldn't have bad-mouthed the Pestletail at all, and you are 100% right, here's why.<br /> <br /> For animals with a &lt;10 attack pool for any attack, with Lunar shapeshifting, that is automatically (given optimization) a 11 pool (based on max Dex + 5 Brawl + 1 Accuracy), 14 with stunting and an applicable Speciality.<br /> <br /> 14 Dice (18 for the 4 mote, below anima flaring boost) is a whole heck of lot of dice to throw if your base damage is 17 (!!) and you aren't Legendary Size (so it's as cheap to turn into a Pestletail as it is to turn into a bear.) For reference, that's almost as much damage as the Earth Shikari and his Artifact Tetsubo with +2 more accuracy for a mere 4 mote commitment.<br /> <br /> Tack on the 17 soak and 10 hardness and the ability to wear Light Armor (because of course you are a Pestletail with high Evasion) and you are basically a lumbering Silver Tank.<br /> <br /> So I'd like to say, if you want to screw stealth and let it all hang out, Pestletail is a damn good form to kill things in. (But of course highly noticeable).<br /> <br /> If people are interested, by the by, I could walk through the rest of the animals and grade them for aspiring Lunar Shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'd like to note that a cat's low soak can be mitigated with moonsilver armor (probably light to keep your evasion high). Just for the mental image of a cat in a suit of silver armor. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/go45jyvb18hkitv/23.jpg?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Moonsilver armor is going to be great for the high Soak critters. For the Pestletail it's a resting soak of 22 (!!) with Artifact Light. Cat soak is less impressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of animals have merits+special attacks interacting with grapples. I wonder if there's any pattern of shifting forms with Quicksilver Second Face to take advantage of a bunch of these.<br /> <br /> Edit: the best of these are on River Dragons and Tyrant Lizards, who are legendary size. Unless shapeshifting resets mauling bite, the best I found is be a Death Moa/Angler Lizard, grapple someone at short range, and then turn into a bear or great cat for mauling bite. Maybe there's some value to switching between River Dragon and Tyrant Lizard using Behemoth-and-Flea Mastery to use a death roll followed by a ferocious bite followed by a deadly thrash? </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, you've clearly lapped me here, I hadn't even started to consider grappling (mostly because as you said the best forms are the Legendary Sized ones, whereas I've just been thinking about day to day DB 'killin). Good point through, cycling through forms might be a necessity for the consumate animal form combatant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:20:02-08:00","id":1290793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290779#post1290779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean wonky as not sufficiently clear (i.e. they should not require repeated questions for clarification) and, for me, creating a significant, immersion breaking gulf between the rules and the flavour of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And your examples of awesome scenes are probably the scenes I liked least from both of those films.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think it's because it just <i>feels</i> wrong to me. Surprise turning into a bear for combat is awesome. Getting your butt kicked by a little girl because she's secretly a kung fu badass is cool. Getting slaughtered by a housecat because of some dice shenanigans based on pools from a completely different shape is... less awesome. </div> </div> </div>I thought they were awesome and so is Death Kitty (IMHO) and by the by, dice shennanigans is literally like 50% of Exalted, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> But to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:22:26-08:00","id":1290794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290790#post1290790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/go45jyvb18hkitv/23.jpg?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Moonsilver armor is going to be great for the high Soak critters. For the Pestletail it's a resting soak of 22 (!!) with Artifact Light. Cat soak is less impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) this picture made my day. Thank you.<br /> B) I worry that 22 soak is just excessive. Most of the time, 17 soak will reduce your enemy to minimum damage. I guess there are some enemies who can hit 18+ damage, but you pretty much need some kind of damage-boosting charm, and not one that boosts post-soak damage. OTOH, If you have moon silver armor, the only cost to wearing it is being more obviously a lunar, and that ship may have sailed when the pestletail started dodging arrows. Cats will nearly always be in a position to reduce the damage they take, though not by enough to not need to rely on defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:29:41-08:00","id":1290799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290793#post1290793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I thought they were awesome and so is Death Kitty (IMHO) and by the by, dice shennanigans is literally like 50% of Exalted, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> But to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice shenanigans like &quot;I'm an awesome swordsman, I'm rolling a ton of dice and rerolling ones&quot; and &quot;I'm in the form of a cat, but I'm rolling a dice pool like I'm a human&quot; just don't feel the same as each other to me, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:33:32-08:00","id":1290801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290799#post1290799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dice shenanigans like &quot;I'm an awesome swordsman, I'm rolling a ton of dice and rerolling ones&quot; and &quot;I'm in the form of a cat, but I'm rolling a dice pool like I'm a human&quot; just don't feel the same as each other to me, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is literally baked into the rules of Lunar Shapeshifting..? Unless you have a Merit that messes with your dice pools (see Miniscule Creature) you can always roll with your Human Dice Pool, Raitons and Snakes can attack with (not quite kitty level) massive accuracy bonuses?<br /> <br /> So yeah, I guess Lunar Shapeshifting might not be for you then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:40:04-08:00","id":1290803,"title":"","content":"Baked into it now, as of, what, less than a week? And I fail to see any reason why, thematically, it's a core part of Lunar shapeshifting. The fact other people have voiced some concerns would hopefully imply I'm not some lone nutter that just hates the idea of Lunars changing shape (I hope not, otherwise what the hell have I been playing for the last five years or so?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:07:06-08:00","id":1290813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290213#post1290213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ask the Devs thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page1058\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-devs/page1058</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the link!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:09:53-08:00","id":1290816,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I'm not convinced by the tiny creatures for combat.<br /> <br /> My totem form is a viper.<br /> If I do a withering attack with my hands, I have +4 accuracy and do 11 damage.<br /> If I take viper form and do a withering attack, I have +1 accuracy and do 3 damage.<br /> <br /> Sure, I'm not that bad at hitting (well, 9 dice vs 15 dice, but that's because I can't use Snake Style as a snake; anyway, theoretically it's only 3 less), but with 3 damage, I'm just going to be pinging. And other small animals are the same.<br /> <br /> Now, there is some value in sneaking (with double 9s for Camouflage, and the enemy losing 2 successes) up to someone and biting them with the initiative from my Join Battle (7 dice, +3 successes, so let's say 7 initiative). And I'll do a bit of damage. But more importantly, poison them.<br /> <br /> And yes, then they are attacking me and I get +2 Evasion, but Dodge is expensive compared to Brawl (as Brawl gives you Parry and attack) so my Evasion isn't that good anyway, and I could always spend 4m to get the same effect.<br /> <br /> But then... how am I going to get more Initiative with a Withering damage of 3?<br /> <br /> All in all, the snake form seems good for sneaking up and biting people, but not after that. Which seems... fair, tbh?<br /> <br /> A housecat can't even poison people. It's bite has a Withering of 4. Your accuracy is 3 less than a punch; yeah, you make it up on a surprise attack, but that's charm dice anyway.<br /> Yeah, they're hot shit at grappling... mice. Rats.<br /> They can't grapple people.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you get the two Latent abilities, they're good, but that's 12xp, you could have bought a charm and a half for that and not needed latent abilities just to do attacks.<br /> <br /> All-in-all, if you're really keen on killing people as a housecat, you can. It's not a very powerful choice though.<br /> <br /> Easier to do it as a Tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-22-2019, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:19:19-08:00","id":1290821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290816#post1290816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you guys mentioned how rubbish the damage is on small animals? I didn't see that come up.<br /> <br /> My totem form is a viper.<br /> If I do a withering attack with my hands, I have +4 accuracy and do 11 damage.<br /> If I take viper form and do a withering attack, I have +1 accuracy and do 3 damage.<br /> <br /> Sure, I'm not that bad at hitting (well, 9 dice vs 15 dice, but that's because I can't use Snake Style as a snake; anyway, theoretically it's only 3 less), but with 3 damage, I'm just going to be pinging. And other small animals are the same.<br /> <br /> Now, there is some value in sneaking (with double 9s for Camouflage, and the enemy losing 2 successes) up to someone and biting them with the initiative from my Join Battle (7 dice, +3 successes, so let's say 7 initiative). And I'll do a bit of damage. But more importantly, poison them.<br /> <br /> And yes, then they are attacking me and I get +2 Evasion, but Dodge is expensive compared to Brawl (as Brawl gives you Parry and attack) so my Evasion isn't that good anyway, and I could always spend 4m to get the same effect.<br /> <br /> But then... how am I going to get more Initiative with a Withering damage of 3?<br /> <br /> All in all, the snake form seems good for sneaking up and biting people, but not after that. Which seems... fair, tbh?<br /> <br /> A housecat can't even poison people. It's bite has a Withering of 4. Your accuracy is 3 less than a punch; yeah, you make it up on a surprise attack, but that's charm dice anyway.<br /> Yeah, they're hot shit at grappling... mice. Rats.<br /> They can't grapple people.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you get the two Latent abilities, they're good, but that's 12xp, you could have bought a charm and a half for that and not needed latent abilities just to do attacks.<br /> <br /> All-in-all, if you're really keen on killing people as a housecat, you can. It's not a very powerful choice though.<br /> <br /> Easier to do it as a Tiger.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the 2 Latents, Housecats have the highest accuracy I've found in the core rulebook (I don't own the other sources of critters) at +14, pre stunting and specialty and comparable damage to the Big Cat. They also have that +2 EV passive which is better than most Ess 1 Dexterity Charms for raising EV and also happens to eat successes to notice them in Stealth.<br /> <br /> Their damage is decent (with the latent). Its really just a good all rounder for the Dex Build (if you want to go loud, Pestletail is better than the Big Cat I've realized now)<br /> <br /> Great Cats are not bad, but they suffer from the poor-ish defence if you are using their animal dice pool (and if you use your human dice pool, the housecat has a +1 EV advantage all the time and a +2 EV advantage most of the time), are not as accurate if you are dex focused and are rather hard to use in as many situations compared to the Housecat? A decent shape for a non-combat focused Lunar, I guess.<br /> <br /> I fully agree that some investments need to be made to make the Houecat a true terror, but they are very good, I feel, after that.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, just to add so I can be clear with regards to my biases. Death Kitty. The entertainment value is over 9000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-22-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:04:49-08:00","id":1290833,"title":"","content":"I would like to note that the Lunar Dexterity Subterfuge section has a number of charms with Protean benefits that key off the Ambush Hunter merit or the Tiny Creature merit.<br /> <br /> Death Kitty is looking like a very, very nice build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:07:00-08:00","id":1290834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290779#post1290779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean wonky as not sufficiently clear (i.e. they should not require repeated questions for clarification) and, for me, creating a significant, immersion breaking gulf between the rules and the flavour of the game.<br /> <br /> And your examples of awesome scenes are probably the scenes I liked least from both of those films.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think it's because it just <i>feels</i> wrong to me. Surprise turning into a bear for combat is awesome. Getting your butt kicked by a little girl because she's secretly a kung fu badass is cool. Getting slaughtered by a housecat because of some dice shenanigans based on pools from a completely different shape is... less awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two opinions on this:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I personally found the rules intuitive and they really aren\u2019t that wonky if you don\u2019t over read and put what you want in them. As intended and hopefully clarified given feedback the rules are pretty straight forward. I mean I actually got confused a bit early on in this thread because I felt like people were seeing rules I didn\u2019t so to speak and thought I must have been misreading them.</li> <li>I think your personal taste shouldn\u2019t dictate other people\u2019s fun. If Prototype00 and honestly myself find the idea of a little cat killer to be fun (and hilarious) then perhaps the rules are working as written. Besides to get his example to work you have to buy two latent abilities (12 experience) so I feel like if you are investing experience in a form then of course you get cool bonuses, no different than evocations.</li> </ol>Also looking at the vast majority of animals in the core book most are far from broken, most are just middle of the road beasties if not mediocre. I will restate my opinion that in all reality that most animal forms are better for secondary combatants or ranged persons that have lost their distance advantage. If they are willing to invest some of their Lunar Experience into latent abilities then they should gain some advantage. If you really invest into shapeshifting combat as your shtick buying charms and latent abilities to support that then I see no problem with these rules as they stand now. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:36:50-08:00","id":1290850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290790#post1290790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If people are interested, by the by, I could walk through the rest of the animals and grade them for aspiring Lunar Shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be interesting to see, however that is a bunch of animals! If you got the time go for it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:01:34-08:00","id":1290862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290834#post1290834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]I personally found the rules intuitive and they really aren\u2019t that wonky if you don\u2019t over read and put what you want in them. As intended and hopefully clarified given feedback the rules are pretty straight forward. I mean I actually got confused a bit early on in this thread because I felt like people were seeing rules I didn\u2019t so to speak and thought I must have been misreading them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad they were clear to you, and I certainly hope they are clear to everyone come publication but it seems evident not everyone found them intuitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290834#post1290834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]I think your personal taste shouldn\u2019t dictate other people\u2019s fun. If Prototype00 and honestly myself find the idea of a little cat killer to be fun (and hilarious) then perhaps the rules are working as written. Besides to get his example to work you have to buy two latent abilities (12 experience) so I feel like if you are investing experience in a form then of course you get cool bonuses, no different than evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I apologise if you found that my not liking the idea and having some concerns about the mechanics and the result they may have on the game may be came across as declaring that your fun was somehow wrong. By all means murder kitty your way across Creation and have a whale of a time. But at the same time your fun does not have to be my fun, and your enjoyment should not dictate that I should not be able to voice my own opinion on things, I'm sure we can agree?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:46:14-08:00","id":1290879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290862#post1290862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I apologise if you found that my not liking the idea and having some concerns about the mechanics and the result they may have on the game may be came across as declaring that your fun was somehow wrong. By all means murder kitty your way across Creation and have a whale of a time. But at the same time your fun does not have to be my fun, and your enjoyment should not dictate that I should not be able to voice my own opinion on things, I'm sure we can agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fair. Really only house cats seem to have this particular set up, all the other animals seem pretty balanced. Given the charms we just seen today I would be much more fearful of a Lunar martial artist then killer kitten since they can stack native charms and martial arts charms. <br /> <br /> That said I really think this is the set up for a really cool trickster character. A black cat, a omen of bad luck, the cute lil kitty that tricks and bedevils those around it and wreaks horror when irritated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:04:24-08:00","id":1290884,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something, but it seems like Death Kitty's attacks aren't any more powerful than a normal light weapon Unarmed attack? At that point you're really just using the form for the Evasion bonus and ambush /shock potential. Which, given that you have to spend 12 exp on latent abilities to get there doesn't seem to be a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T14:56:48-08:00","id":1290911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290821#post1290821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the 2 Latents, Housecats have the highest accuracy I've found in the core rulebook (I don't own the other sources of critters) at +14, pre stunting and specialty and comparable damage to the Big Cat. They also have that +2 EV passive which is better than most Ess 1 Dexterity Charms for raising EV and also happens to eat successes to notice them in Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The great cat has a base damage of 16 on their bite vs the 12 of the Housecat. I don't see this as comparable, especially once you go against armoured opponents Consider medium artifact armour with 3 stamina. This gives 11 soak. Your 12 damage is reduced to 1, while the 16 of the great cat is reduced to 5. On top of this they cat has leaping pounce, potentially enabling the ability to reflexively grapple. They also get +4 damage on savaging decisive attacks with mauling bite.<br /> <br /> A base damage of 12 without overwhelming is definitely on the low end against the kind of opponents exalted are expected to face. You have fixated so much on the mote efficiency for the accuracy/evasion bonus that you have picked an animal that you are going to need to spend motes to be able to deal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T15:07:19-08:00","id":1290913,"title":"","content":"Yeah, even a bronze sword and strength 3 is more damage.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't think it's rubbish. I can see where protype00 is coming from. If you really love the idea of the deathkitty, you can.<br /> <br /> I just don't think it's that powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T18:54:13-08:00","id":1290957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290764#post1290764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do people not like the idea of a small, underestimated creature absolutely dominating combat I wonder?</div> </div> </div> </div>EX3 combat is a collaberative effort between player and storyteller, there are ways you can go for comedy at the expense of my NPCs that will make me regret the effort I put into creating them, in that regard a cat's actually on the more respectable end of this because its not (for example) a rodent scaling their trouser leg to attack their groin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:39:54-08:00","id":1291027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290957#post1290957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EX3 combat is a collaberative effort between player and storyteller, there are ways you can go for comedy at the expense of my NPCs that will make me regret the effort I put into creating them, in that regard a cat's actually on the more respectable end of this because its not (for example) a rodent scaling their trouser leg to attack their groin.</div> </div> </div> </div>And vice-versa; if the Storyteller is getting miffed that a player is going out of his way to defeat the Abyssal boss fight as a tabby cat, imagine the fury of the Night Caste's player when his character gets tossed around by a Lunar in ant form like Loki getting thrashed by the Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T02:29:24-08:00","id":1291051,"title":"","content":"Death Kitty is certainly nice, not to mention fun, if you invested in those 2 latents, with a truly impressive base defense but it won't dominate the game. For that the damage is too low. It misses the cannon part of glass cannon. As for accuracy, a pack hunter who learns the latent to apply this to his human allies can add up to 3 successes to his attack roll (and after 1 wp, 3 on raw damage of decisives), so I must contest that death kitty is far from the most accurate of animals. Also, the pack hunters generally add distract gambit shenanigans which are supported by native charms, and some like the wolves/dogs even add in free defend others with complimentary counterattacks (though much less damage than claw striders).<br /> <br /> Also, there are so many great grapple latents! For example a bear can open with 'Crushing Bear Hug' on a withering attack, allowing a follow-up reflexive grapple with an accuracy boost. Learn 'Crushing Embrace', giving that a follow-up decisive attack with raw damage equal to the extra successes on your control roll which ignores hardness and doesn't reset. Add 'Mauling Bite' for good measure. Now that's a solid way to open combat, with a thoroughly mauled opponent in your loving embrace! And we have yet to see the Strength Charms!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the flyers! A Death Diving, Eagle with Swooping Descent &amp; Peck out the Eyes has +4 accuracy, +2 successes on that first attack roll from stealth, double 10's on damage &amp; can forgo one damage to blind. That is also a really nice way to start (or finish) combat!<br /> <br /> And with all their intimidation charms lunars have yet another way to do truly wicked stuff. Take the Gorilla: can do join battle with intimidation thanks to Howling Aggression, and you go first anyway if you beat their resolve. Add Predators Menace so all successes over resolve also reduce their intitiative and, well, you have entire charm trees dedicated to be scary, so, eh, solid odds for crashing them while rolling join battle. Oh, and much grappling goodness such as mauling bite and savaging strength, so see above. Merciful kami, gorillas will be very, very scary lunar opponents...<br /> <br /> Ok, and that was just me looking till 'Gorilla'. I'm convinced Death Kitty will be one scary, awesome, deeply troubling house cat, yes, but then again it's a Lunar housecat, so yeah. It's still best suited for sneaking and infiltration and there are some much more effective animals for general mayhem and destruction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:36:16-08:00","id":1291155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1290911#post1290911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The great cat has a base damage of 16 on their bite vs the 12 of the Housecat. I don't see this as comparable, especially once you go against armoured opponents Consider medium artifact armour with 3 stamina. This gives 11 soak. Your 12 damage is reduced to 1, while the 16 of the great cat is reduced to 5. On top of this they cat has leaping pounce, potentially enabling the ability to reflexively grapple. They also get +4 damage on savaging decisive attacks with mauling bite.<br /> <br /> A base damage of 12 without overwhelming is definitely on the low end against the kind of opponents exalted are expected to face. You have fixated so much on the mote efficiency for the accuracy/evasion bonus that you have picked an animal that you are going to need to spend motes to be able to deal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, even a bronze sword and strength 3 is more damage.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't think it's rubbish. I can see where protype00 is coming from. If you really love the idea of the deathkitty, you can.<br /> <br /> I just don't think it's that powerful. </div> </div> </div>I've thought about this and reviewed the stats and:<br /> <br /> 1. You are completely right and I was probably fixating on it a tad too much.<br /> <br /> 2. Don't know why my eyes glazed over big cat bite damage, dang!<br /> <br /> Revised rules for decent shapeshift options for day to day use:<br /> <br /> 1. You probably want to avoid the Legendary Sized stuff except for emergencies as A. Super obvious and B. Not Mote Efficient.<br /> <br /> 2. You probably want something with an attack with crap accuracy (&lt;10 dice for accuracy), but big damage (15+). Then you can sub in your own dice pool and pick up a +1 accuracy to it on top. Sans all else, you get a 14 accuracy pool pre-merits and mote expenditure if you count stunting and a relevant specialty. In this specific category (&lt;10 accuracy 15+ damage) we have:<br /> <br /> - Bear (Bite 15 damage)<br /> - Benthic Knifetooth (Bite 15 damage)<br /> <b>- Boar Tusk Crocodile (Bite 16 damage)</b><br /> - Bunyip (Headbutt 15 damage)<br /> - Claw Strider (Bite 15 damage)<br /> - Death Moa (Peck 15 damage)<br /> <b>- Gorilla (Bite 16 damage)<br /> - Great Cat (Bite 16 damage)<br /> - Pestletail (Tail Slam 17 damage, Minimum 4)</b><br /> <br /> As you can see if you want to get the most out of your specialty (Vance's recommendation is that you can select one type of attack), you'd want a Brawl Specialty for Bite, which gets you the superior accuracy on the Boar Tusk Crocodile, the Great Cat and the Gorilla and you just miss the gold standard of the Pestletail (which you have to take a specific specialty for, I don't think any other animal has a Tail Slam.)<br /> <br /> It's late and I don't have time to go through all the cases mentioned above, but lets look at the four I highlighted.<br /> <br /> <b>Boar Tusk Crocodile:</b><br /> <br /> A very decent combat form thanks to high soak (13/0) and this merit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crushing Bite: The three elongated fangs that give the<br /> boar-tusk crocodile its name have formidable biting pressure.<br /> Any withering bite attack it makes ignores up to<br /> four points of soak, plus an additional point of soak for<br /> each extra success on the attack roll. This cannot reduce<br /> an enemy\u2019s soak below his (Stamina). </div> </div> </div>If you boost your accuracy on your attack, this is liable to reduce your opponent's soak by a considerable amount. They also seem to have a sideline in knocking prone (smashing snout) and dealing bonus Decisive damage but I'm not sure how useful this tactic would be given how easy it is to rise from prone, even with foes at close range (difficulty 2).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Killing Strike: The boar-tusk crocodile takes down prey<br /> by ramming them to the ground, then biting at their<br /> exposed vitals. Any decisive bite attack it makes against<br /> a prone enemy adds +5 raw damage </div> </div> </div>I'd probably just stick to the damaging, soak bypassing bite and very decent soak to see me through fights.<br /> <br /> The Boar Tusk Crocodile has no specific defense merit or latents, and you'll have to depend on base parry/dodge pool and whatever Lunar Charms you have, which I would advise investing in.<br /> <br /> <b>Gorilla:</b><br /> <br /> As mentioned (not by me) Gorillas can roll Intimidate to Join Battle (so should be good for Cha Lunars),<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Howling Aggression: A gorilla may Join Battle with its<br /> intimidation dice pool, attempting to frighten enemies<br /> into fleeing by shaking large tree branches, beating its<br /> chest, or baring fangs. It may take its turn on the first<br /> round before that of any enemy whose Resolve was overcome<br /> by the roll, regardless of its actual Initiative rating. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how it interacts with this universal latent though:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Predator\u2019s Menace: Animals with an intimidate pool can<br /> be trained with this attack, causing an intimidated enemy<br /> to lose Initiative equal to the extra successes over his<br /> Resolve, even if he pays Willpower to resist. Once per scene. </div> </div> </div>If the ability to join battle using Intimidation pool is actually a Threaten attempt, then all well and good, if not, we'll have to find some other way to threaten, maybe Poised Lion Attitude?<br /> <br /> Gorillas are also great grapplers (if you are going the pure Dex route, no worries, you can just use their native 10 dice, 10 dice to control pool and this Latent to guarantee yourself at least 5 successes on the control roll)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Savaging Strength (Latent): A gorilla that has been trained<br /> for combat can put its strength to use in denying enemies<br /> escape. It may pay a point of Willpower to convert up to five<br /> dice on the control roll of a clinch to automatic successes. </div> </div> </div>This latent:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crushing Embrace: Large predators that rely on clinching<br /> can be trained to make a decisive savaging attack upon<br /> grappling an enemy, with raw damage equal to the extra<br /> successes on control roll. This attack ignores hardness<br /> and does not reset the animal to base Initiative. Once<br /> per scene. </div> </div> </div>and Mauling Bite:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mauling Bite: When the gorilla makes a decisive bite<br /> attack against a clinched enemy, it adds +4 to the raw<br /> damage of this attack. It can receive this bonus only once<br /> per clinch, unless reset by crashing the clinched enemy. </div> </div> </div>Will allow you to take two quite damaging decisives on any grappled target.<br /> <br /> The Gorilla has no specific defense merit or latents, and you'll have to depend on base parry/dodge pool and whatever Lunar Charms you have, which I would advise investing in. Worse, it's soak is 6/0, so you will definitely need your Moonsilver armor for this form.<br /> <br /> <b>Great Cat:</b><br /> <br /> Great Cats are all about attacking from Stealth and moving into close range, attacking with their weaker claw attack (12 damage as opposed to 16 damage on the bite) and hoping for 5+ levels of Withering Damage and a free grapple, otherwise quite similar to Gorilla, sans the Intimidate shennanigans. (They even have mauling bite).<br /> <br /> I dunno, I kind of like the straight forward nature of the gorilla's Intimidate - grapple - Crush - bite repeat strategy better, but thats just me.<br /> <br /> Great cats actually have a defensive merit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Battle Cat (Latent): Great cats in the wild rely on ambush<br /> tactics to take down weaker prey, and generally avoid<br /> animals capable of fighting back against them. With training,<br /> they can be taught to defend against the tactics of<br /> trained combatants, adding +1 Evasion against any attack<br /> made by an enemy with lower Initiative and +1 Evasion<br /> against any attack made from medium range or further.<br /> These bonuses stack. </div> </div> </div>So if you're winning, you're going to be harder to hit, still at Soak of 6/0 and a situational EV boost, I would recommend Moonsilver armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Pestletail:</b><br /> <br /> I've made my feelings on the Pestletail really clear, it is one of my favorite forms because it has the most damaging attack of non Kaiju forms and the most soak too. It also has 4 (!!) defensive soak oriented merits/latents which makes it a much more survivable form (good merits too):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bony Shell: Withdrawing into its heavy shell affords a<br /> pestletail extraordinary defense. It may take Full Defense<br /> actions without losing any Initiative. In addition, Full<br /> Defense actions add four to the pestletail\u2019s soak and hardness<br /> as well as increasing its Defense. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Impenetrable Armor: The minimum damage of any<br /> withering attack made against the pestletail is reduced<br /> by one die, to a minimum of zero. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sturdy as Stone: A pestletail cannot be knocked back or<br /> prone except by magical effects and by creatures of extraordinary<br /> size, such as tyrant lizards. Similarly, a grappled<br /> pestletail cannot be thrown or slammed unless magic<br /> such as Dragon Coil Technique is used, or if the grappling<br /> creature is gigantic. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hardened Shell Superiority (Latent): Whenever a withering<br /> attack against the pestletail fails to deal any damage,<br /> the attacker loses a point of Initiative which is granted to<br /> the beast. Whenever a decisive attack fails to damage it,<br /> the pestletail gains an Initiative Break of 5 points </div> </div> </div>And you can pseudo Heaven Thunder Hammer with it's tail during Decisives for even more damage (falling damage is no joke in Exalted. This potentially, with the base Decisive damage, could one hit TKO even most Exalts)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Smashing Tail Hammer (Latent): The pestletail may pay<br /> a point of Willpower before making a decisive tail slam<br /> attack to grant the attack the benefits of the Solar Charm<br /> Heaven Thunder Hammer if it hits. Using Smashing Tail<br /> Hammer counts as making a smashing attack, and incurs<br /> the additional Defense penalty for such. </div> </div> </div>Man, I love the Pestletail.<br /> <br /> Well, thats it, I'm sure I missed something, but I'm feeling more confident about playing a Dex focused Shifter Lunar who maybe splashes Str for Grapple charms (or not if going Pestletail). If you want it to be your main combat style though, Latent purchase is probably necessary.<br /> <br /> I'll pick up with other animals next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-23-2019, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:52:46-08:00","id":1291402,"title":"","content":"On yet even more reflection, it occurs to me that the Boar Tusked Crocodile form probably edges out the Pestletail if you want pure offence thanks to that -4 or more soak attack of its, giving it an effective (at least, if not more) 20 L damage attack as long as the antagonist has at least 4 soak. <br /> <br /> Pre any Charms.<br /> <br /> That will be hard to stand up to.... <br /> <br /> For next post for some variety, I might go through the charms and see which are best for a shifter combatant (out of Dex, mainly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T01:09:47-08:00","id":1291450,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I just realized while doing some reading for Charm recommendations that you could, if you took the following Charm:<br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lunar\u2019s true self transcends definition, manifesting itself as a chimerical combination of beasts. She permanently alters her spirit shape by granting it aspects of a second animal, applying six dots of mutations based on that animal. These mutations also automatically apply when she uses Hybrid Body Transformation. The Lunar treats both animals as her spirit shape for Totemic Charms. </div> </div> </div>You could take 6 points of mutation for your spirit shape, which could include:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prehensile Tongue/Trunk (\u2022\u2022) \u2014 Innate<br /> The character has a prehensile trunk, tongue, or similar appendage, which acts as a fully functional limb, though it suffers a \u22121 offhand penalty. It has light weapon traits (Accuracy +4, Damage +7, Defense +0, Overwhelming 1), with the Bashing, Brawl, Disarming, Flexible, Grappling, and Natural tags. </div> </div> </div>The only reason I menion this is that on Death Kitty (now Displacer Kitty, I suppose), this particular mutation will probably be more effective than their natural bite attack (and save you on purchasing a Latent), and also bring their native accuracy back up to 20 with the Ambidexterous (O) merit.<br /> <br /> Downside is, you require 5 Str and look like a mutated freak kitten, and so that is bad for concealment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T01:52:43-08:00","id":1291455,"title":"","content":"So Charms for the Consumate Shifter (i.e. someone who wants to fight with those sweet, sweet animal form bonuses all the time.) I'm just going to focus on E1 charms as they are whats important for Character Creation.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Universal</b></u><br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression: Add 6 more mutation points from another animal to your base spirit shape form. Not bad, not bad at all, though based on what you choose, you could stand out just a smidge.<br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Transformation: Useful for your human form, of course, but I would choose defensive or utility mutations as most of your combat will be done in critter form.<br /> <br /> Shifting Beast Nature: Eh, it's a separate pool of mutations for your HBT and you can switch between the as a misc action for free. Its not bad, if you have a concrete use in mind for it (i.e. talky HBT and Utility HBT)<br /> <br /> Many-Faced Moon Transformation: Is useful, for disguising, which every Lunar should be good at, not just Shifters.<br /> <br /> <b>Quicksilver Second Face</b>: Pure gold, you definitely want to take this. For 2i you get to shift into another form (for no motes, it seems) at any point on your turn. Attack in your bitey form and then transform into your defensive form (Pestletail! Death Kitty!) for massive evasion/soak before you end your turn. A must have pick.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dexterity</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Shapeshifting:</b><br /> <br /> Heart's Blood, Nest Raiding Slyness: The only Heart's Blood Option that works on animals previewed thus far. For all you animal lovers out there, you don't have to kill them, you just have to be a massive jerk. Woohoo! (Probably pretty good)<br /> <br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form: To turn into a literal fly on the wall. You aren't going to kill anybody in this form, but if there was a charm for Perfect Spying, this would be it.<br /> <br /> <b>Offense:</b><br /> <br /> Finding the Needle's Eye: A bit situational, but will be very nice if your foe is behind partial cover (or even full cover!)<br /> <br /> Coyote-And-Badger Technique: Depends, do you want to kick ass yourself, if so this is not so great, or do you want to set up your friend's Decisive? Even so, I'm not too fond for this build.<br /> <br /> Weapon Snatching Coils: Disarm is a pretty good tactic against certain Exalted foes, and if you are a Pestletail, this becomes super good to use (you basically get to toss the weapon really far away reflexively)<br /> <br /> <b>Striking Mospid Method</b>: A very good bread and butter to reroll 3 failed dice on a withering attack making your bite super accurate.<br /> <br /> <b>Foe Driving Attack</b>: Again another accuracy booster, this time by increasing onslaught penalty. Not too expensive either.<br /> <br /> Many-Armed Warrior Panoply, Needle Quill Technique, Bombardier Spittle Alchemy, Stinging Ichneumon Scourge: Actually super bad for you, animal forms don't use weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Sinuous Striking Grace</b>: Pseudo +5 (based on max Dex) to your Init to determine who goes first, if you hit an enemy who hasn't gone yet +1 non charm dice to accuracy. Not bad, but take Striking Mospid Method first. Go-first is of course a powerful tactic.<br /> <br /> Cunning Beast Warrior Reflexes: The Flurry better charm (only -2 penalty on both actions, no defense penalty). I am trying to think what would be a good action to flurry with attacks in general and am drawing a blank, anyone want to enlighten me? Otherwise it is situational.<br /> <br /> Wasp Sting Blur: If your foe is suffering a bunch of Onslaught, you can really make them hurt with this charm. A bit situational as there haven't been any multi-attack charms as of yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Agile Beast Defence</b>: Bread and butter defensive charm and it's great! Especially if you become Death Kitty at the end of your turn. With this charm and a 4m expenditure to boost your Evasion, you can end up with a 12 EV (if you maxed Dodge).<br /> <br /> <b>Bending Before the Storm</b>: Here is your onslaught negator if you are Higher Init than your foes. Its not bad, and quite early on in the defense tree. If you don't have higher init, its still quite good.<br /> <br /> <b>Ferocious Guardian Beast Defence</b>: Makes you very good at defend another actions (which are reflexive now) Probably a must pick, especially if you have either 12 EV (Death Kitty) or 22 Soak (Pestletail with Moonsilver Armor).<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Tiger Stance</b>: Ooh, potentially 13 EV Death Kitty! I like it.<br /> <br /> Coiled Serpent Strikes: A reflexive Decisive counterattack on a miss is not bad. I'll have to think about how best to build up the Init quickly, Full Moons have that 1/day anima ability if you want to Decisive twice in a turn.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not done yet, but will probably put the rest in another post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T07:17:04-08:00","id":1291524,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Dexterity (cont.)</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Mobility</b><br /> <br /> Graceful Crane Stance: Actually just a copy of the Solar one, but imagining a full sized two ton Pestletail running across the treetops on it's tip-toes is hilarious. Good utility.<br /> <br /> Cat-footed Grace: Rise from prone (basically guaranteed) as a reflexive action. Good utility, but the Pestletail is mostly immune to prone, remember that.<br /> <br /> Wind-dancing Method: Hmm, I guess this is good for if it is your off turn and you are falling, but if it is your turn, why not just become a bird?<br /> <br /> Instinct Driven Beast Movement: Auto success for 2m for any movement is not bad, especially if the foe is trying to get away.<br /> <br /> Spider Climbing Attitude: Literal spider-man charm. Or if you want to see a Pestletail climb a cave wall upside down. Utility, as before.<br /> <br /> <b>Wounded Beast Flight</b>: Oh, this isn't bad, for emergency getaways, if you need to withdraw from combat (which you will, eventually. There are so many Dragonblooded) definitely worth keeping in your back pocket.<br /> <br /> Swift Killer Style: I desperately want to love this charm, moving one range band away reflexively after attacking is so cool, but you've already used your move, so this doesn't set up skirmisher harrassment unless you are in an aquatic or aerial form and then it cost a WP per use. Someone please tell me I'm missing what makes this charm great?<br /> <br /> Shifting Octopus Trick: Automatically escape from mundane restraints, be very good at escaping from magical restraints. Once again good utility.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Armor Approach: Don armor quickly. Eh, seems slightly situational.<br /> <br /> <b>Subterfuge</b><br /> <br /> Skipping most of this, it does what it says on the tin, mostly. Lunars be good at stealth, take this tree if you want a stealthy Lunar.<br /> <br /> Night Stalker Approach: As long as you are hidden, you can spend as many motes as you like, all muted. Bodes well for spying charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Swarm</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cunning Anglerfish Decoy</b>: Okay, this create an actual combat decoy, ninja style. It's good for a getaway, as if the enemy can't beat your guile, they automatically target the wrong one, but otherwise it is a Simple action so use in attack is limited. About as good as Wounded Beast Flight.<br /> <br /> Phew! Thats all of Dex. If I was just dabbling in combat (but had maxxed Dex and Brawl), I'd take the following:<br /> <br /> <u>Shifter Combat Suite:</u><br /> <br /> <b>Quicksilver Second Face</b>: Pure gold, you definitely want to take this. For 2i you get to shift into another form (for no motes, it seems) at any point on your turn. Attack in your bitey form and then transform into your defensive form (Pestletail! Death Kitty!) for massive evasion/soak before you end your turn. A must have pick.<br /> <br /> <b>Striking Mospid Method</b>: A very good bread and butter to reroll 3 failed dice on a withering attack making your bite super accurate.<br /> <br /> <b>Agile Beast Defence</b>: Bread and butter defensive charm and it's great! Especially if you become Death Kitty at the end of your turn. With this charm and a 4m expenditure to boost your Evasion, you can end up with a 12 EV (if you maxed Dodge).<br /> <br /> <b>Bending Before the Storm</b>: Here is your onslaught negator if you are Higher Init than your foes. Its not bad, and quite early on in the defense tree. If you don't have higher init, its still quite good.<br /> <br /> <b>Wounded Beast Flight</b>: Oh, this isn't bad, for emergency getaways, if you need to withdraw from combat (which you will, eventually. There are so many Dragonblooded) definitely worth keeping in your back pocket.<br /> <br /> These five charms and a good Heart's Blood library (I'd try at least to have the Pestletail, the Cat and the Boar toothed crocodile) will probably make you quite a fearsome combatant even with such a minimal investment in Dex charms.<br /> <br /> Str might have it's own awesome E1 charms, but it is not a given that Shifters have good strength as it doesn't really play into damage calculation. Sta might see more play.<br /> <br /> Edit: Next, I'm going to review the other attribute charms and see if there is anything extraordinary in the other charmsets. If not I might try making a character, non combat focused and see how much combat viability I can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:16:41-08:00","id":1291548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1291524#post1291524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Quicksilver Second Face</b>: Pure gold, you definitely want to take this. For 2i you get to shift into another form (for no motes, it seems) at any point on your turn. Attack in your bitey form and then transform into your defensive form (Pestletail! Death Kitty!) for massive evasion/soak before you end your turn. A must have pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not read this as replacing the mote cost of shapeshifting. Mostly because Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement explicitly removes the cost, and QSF doesn't mention removing or replacing the cost.<br /> It's still pure gold (moonsilver?).<br /> It's also good for if you have to start of a fight in the middle of a conversation, to skip the otherwise necessary loss of your first turn to shapeshifting..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:53:09-08:00","id":1291637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1291548#post1291548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not read this as replacing the mote cost of shapeshifting. Mostly because Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement explicitly removes the cost, and QSF doesn't mention removing or replacing the cost.<br /> It's still pure gold (moonsilver?).<br /> It's also good for if you have to start of a fight in the middle of a conversation, to skip the otherwise necessary loss of your first turn to shapeshifting..</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, is that the case? Yes then it is necessary for Round 1 turning into murderform if you started from Human, and more final fight/emergency usage.<br /> <br /> Wishlist for Charms in other Attributes:<br /> <br /> - Something to hide moonsilver armor (but still have it apply in combat)<br /> - Something to boost natural weapon damage (probably claws of the silver moon)<br /> - All the Soak Charms<br /> <br /> prototype00<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:14:12-08:00","id":1291647,"title":"","content":"My wishlist involves a Lunar Charm that lets a Lunar appear to someone who says his name three times in a mirror. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:57:36-08:00","id":1291654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1291647#post1291647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My wishlist involves a Lunar Charm that lets a Lunar appear to someone who says his name three times in a mirror. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be sure, I want that charm too. But here I was just listing stuff I would like for the basic combat suite for a Shapeshift Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:14:02-08:00","id":1291657,"title":"","content":"My bad! At this level, Striking Mospid is only one dice rerolled for 3m! Probably not worth it. <br /> <br /> Controversially, I will have to say then my recommendation for starting shifters (for Dex Charms) is to put all your eggs in the defence basket and just depend on your Dex excellency for accuracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-24-2019, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:07:45-08:00","id":1292070,"title":"","content":"So there\u2019s been some discussion about the Lunar Tell and how it is bad for storytelling/ or not.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not here to argue thematics, what I am here to tell you is the Lunar Tell is actually Luna\u2019s Gift to optimisers! <br /> <br /> Why, you ask? Well read what the Tell does, it\u2019s present across all your forms permanently and if you attach it to a mutation, that mutation is on all your forms!<br /> <br /> Imagine being able to fly, forever (wings) or having 5 extra soak (Unusual Hide) on all your forms, amazing! (Pestletails have a resting Soak of 22 with this btw).<br /> <br /> And as a Lunar Exalted, you don\u2019t have to worry about things like always looking like a freak, just take the two Charms in Appearance that Hide your Tell and make your always on mutation Subtle. <br /> <br /> Be sure not to miss this particular trick as a Shifter Lunar, it\u2019s worth its weight in Moonsilver!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:16:34-08:00","id":1292073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1292070#post1292070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there\u2019s been some discussion about the Lunar Tell and how it is bad for storytelling/ or not.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not here to argue thematics, what I am here to tell you is the Lunar Tell is actually Luna\u2019s Gift to optimisers!<br /> <br /> Why, you ask? Well read what the Tell does, it\u2019s present across all your forms permanently and if you attach it to a mutation, that mutation is on all your forms!<br /> <br /> Imagine being able to fly, forever (wings) or having 5 extra soak (Unusual Hide) on all your forms, amazing! (Pestletails have a resting Soak of 22 with this btw).<br /> <br /> And as a Lunar Exalted, you don\u2019t have to worry about things like always looking like a freak, just take the two Charms in Appearance that Hide your Tell and make your always on mutation Subtle.<br /> <br /> Be sure not to miss this particular trick as a Shifter Lunar, it\u2019s worth its weight in Moonsilver!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, at first I was really perturbed at the mutation* carry over using the tell. However the more I thought about it if another lunar gets their five dot sword or armor that shape shifts with beast form then mutation tells aren't all that big of a deal. <br /> <br /> Now though with mutation tells AND chimeras we can make some real, horrifying animal form abominations against nature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -- Oh god it is a pesteltail-squid hybrid... with butterfly wing? <br /> <br /> *and enhancing mutations to boot like venom sacs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:21:24-08:00","id":1292074,"title":"","content":"See, I agree completely with your enthusiasm, but am not sure about enhancing mutations (since those are separate mutations your Tell is not attached to) might be they don\u2019t persist, so better to give them to the really beefy mutations that aren\u2019t multi part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T23:23:57-08:00","id":1292080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1292074#post1292074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I agree completely with your enthusiasm, but am not sure about enhancing mutations (since those are separate mutations your Tell is not attached to) might be they don\u2019t persist, so better to give them to the really beefy mutations that aren\u2019t multi part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance said the upgrades come along too. I will find the quote later but it is in the ask the Devs thread.<br /> <br /> *edit: Here you go, bottom of the page: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page1063\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-devs/page1063</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-26-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T21:29:38-07:00","id":1297637,"title":"","content":"So for a STR 5/Dex 5 murderkitty, why not just use Last Warriors Unity too keep a pair of moonsilver Tiger Claws equiped in your cat form? You'd have the same pools as in your human form, enhanced by cat forms merits (+2 evasion and +3 on all attack rolls vs human size enemies with the latent).<br /> <br /> Also I think people are sleeping on bears, the protean charms for berseker are SWEET. With Terrible Wolverine Onslaught you get +2 succeses and +1 dice on all your attack rolls.<br /> <br /> Also +1 Parry from Ferocious Cub Guardian and Mother Grizzly Attitude stack for +2 parry on all defend other actions. A bear lunar with Galliard merged with Last Warrios Unity and a solar meleeist mate with Courante, Heartsbalm and War Lion Stance are ridiculous. Bear lunar gets +5 Parry scene-long (+1 Cub Guardian, +1 Mother Grizzly, +1 Galliard, +2 Heartsbalm) to defend her solar mate once Relentless Lunar Fury and Heart-Forged Aegis are up, while the solar is 'only' at +3 to parry for the lunar but gets Hail-Shattering Practice. Even a slightly less optimised duo without Heartsbalm is still quite formidable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-18-2019, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T22:07:01-07:00","id":1297642,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well originally I had wanted Death Kitty to do well with just Dex, but that is a not bad idea. I wonder how Claws of the Silver Moon would interact (not at all I\u2019m guessing).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve not thought much about bears, being obsessed with Hippos of late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:31:06-07:00","id":1297843,"title":"","content":"Oh based on Vance's recent reply on Berserker, I seem to actually have underestimated it. Because you apparently still keep the full Berserker bonus even when you negate the wound penalties..<br /> <br /> Even at E1 with just Pain Tolerance and Relentless Lunar Fury, you can have up to +5 to attacks with only -1 effective wound penalty to non-attacks, and at E4 with Terrible Wolverine Onslaught it just goes insane with a +2 successes, up to +5 dice, and no penalty at all to non-attacks. If you don't oneshot the bear/hellboar lunar (hello Untoppable Juggernaut Incarnation) you are in for a world of hurt.<br /> <br /> Also with a hellboar, if you can prone someone, you can throw that attack bonus on an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage of Death Stomps, with +5 decisive damage on every hit. Hellboar also has a lot more merits that key to protean charms, like Trample and a Speed Bonus, so I lean toward them over bears as the best Berserker animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-18-2019, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:42:53-07:00","id":1297846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1297843#post1297843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh based on Vance's recent reply on Berserker, I seem to actually have underestimated it. Because you apparently still keep the full Berserker bonus even when you negate the wound penalties..<br /> <br /> Even at E1 with just Pain Tolerance and Relentless Lunar Fury, you can have up to +5 to attacks with only -1 effective wound penalty to non-attacks, and at E4 with Terrible Wolverine Onslaught it just goes insane with a +2 successes, up to +5 dice, and no penalty at all to non-attacks. If you don't oneshot the bear/hellboar lunar (hello Untoppable Juggernaut Incarnation) you are in for a world of hurt.<br /> <br /> Also with a hellboar, if you can prone someone, you can throw that attack bonus on an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage of Death Stomps, with +5 decisive damage on every hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t that mean that you are on your -4 HL though...? I mean I like dancing on the knife\u2019s edge as much as the next guy, but I also like keeping my insides inside! (All the best Don\u2019t Die Charms are at higher Ess)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:46:40-07:00","id":1297850,"title":"","content":"You can have 11 -4 HLs as an E1 lunar though, and even at -2 you're still at +3 on attacks, and since Relentless Lunar Fury rounds down, no penalty to non-attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-18-2019, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T19:13:12-07:00","id":1297857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1297850#post1297850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have 11 -4 HLs as an E1 lunar though, and even at -2 you're still at +3 on attacks, and since Relentless Lunar Fury rounds down, no penalty to non-attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. Def good for a certain Str Sta build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T21:11:13-07:00","id":1297879,"title":"","content":"Another idea for murderkitty: Last Warriors Unity Weirdflame (Moonsilver Flamecaster) and grab some wings with Chimera-Soul Expression. Ambush Hunter/Underfoot Menace don't have anything that stop them working with ranged weapons and neatly cancel the -3 attack from flying. Weirdflame is a flame weapon so you don't need strength for damage and for Sparks of Madness giving a derangement you're a wyld-powered cat-based flying weapons platform; no one's going to expect you to be sane anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-19-2019, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T22:00:29-07:00","id":1297886,"title":"","content":"Hmm, interesting. I hadn\u2019t thought of Flame Weapons for Death Kitty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T05:44:08-07:00","id":1297933,"title":"","content":"Using a moonsilver devil-caster adds the ability to attack at short range, an additional 4 withing damage and 3 overwhelming damage, accuracy equal or greater to the claw and bite attacks, and the possibility of using evocations. However, you wouldn't be able to use Last Warrior Unity's prerequisite, Ferocious Biting Tooth, to enhance the attacks because the damage wouldn't be enhanced by Strength.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't use Weirdflame, Dexterity has the charms to help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T14:39:24-07:00","id":1298044,"title":"","content":"You also could use a moonsilver powerbow, unless you worry that's too large for a cat to use. You'd need to have a high strength to get as good damage, but you needed a good strength for Last Warrior's Unity, gain access to attack-boosting strength charms, avoid the slow tag, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T16:50:34-07:00","id":1298076,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Last Warrior Unity uses the examples of a Grand Daiklaive (2 handed heavy weapon) merging with a tail and a Dragon Sigh Wand (2 handed Heavy archery weapon) merging with a beak, so I think that would work. In either case I think you would need Needle Quill attack/Bombardier Beetle Alchemy to justify having any ammo i without Weirdflame.<br /> <br /> The advantage of a flame weapon is that you could still have +1 accuracy when at close range, but a powerbow might make for better sniping from stealth. Of course, only a devil caster or artifact hand crossbow would leave with a functional hand when not shapeshifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:09:28-07:00","id":1300224,"title":"","content":"Ok hear me out: Wasps.<br /> <br /> This requires essence 3 or essence 2 with Radiant Basilisc Jewel, because it needs the repurchase of Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery to overcome the wasps poisons low damage, but the wasp does have a big advantage in having a naturally long duration (6 turns) which becomes (9 turns + essence) with Adder Fang, Mamba-and-Cobra, and the Enhanced Toxin merit, and then Mamba-and-Cobra repurchase lets you get 1i+(10s on attack &amp; damage roll) (max 5)<b> aggravated</b> damage on it.<br /> <br /> This is in many ways superior to The Dragon Dies Screaming (in comparison wasp lunar gets +4 duration, on average equal damage attacking with 10i, and lower penalty) from White Veil but instead of 6m 6i 1WP you just pay 3m 2i and you get to do it with Miniscule Size bonuses and flight. Pretty brutal for a lunar assassin.<br /> <br /> Edit: I remembered Vance has said they are going to explicitly allow enhanced toxin mutations to enhance creatures natural venoms so numbers went up.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: This works at E1 with octopi since they dont need the damage boost and only the duration from the first purchase of Mamba-and-Cobra, but if you want to do it on land you need to be some sort of chimeric flying octopus abomination. Being a wasp is just cleaner, though I wish we had like black-widow stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-27-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:58:57-07:00","id":1300251,"title":"","content":"He did? Where?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:30:12-07:00","id":1300265,"title":"","content":"Here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2/page16#post1296751\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...16#post1296751</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sasha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1296733#post1296733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can an animal form with a non-Snake Venom poisoned attack (e.g. octopus, wasp) gain the Enhanced Toxin mutation via charms (e.g. Chimera-Soul Expression, Perfected Hybrid Interaction) despite not technically having the Poisoned Body or Venomous merits?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1296751#post1296751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good; I'll probably tweak the prerequisites to make that work explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T07:28:04-07:00","id":1300276,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T15:49:57-07:00","id":1300404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300224#post1300224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok hear me out: Wasps.<br /> <br /> This requires essence 3 or essence 2 with Radiant Basilisc Jewel, because it needs the repurchase of Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery to overcome the wasps poisons low damage, but the wasp does have a big advantage in having a naturally long duration (6 turns) which becomes (9 turns + essence) with Adder Fang, Mamba-and-Cobra, and the Enhanced Toxin merit, and then Mamba-and-Cobra repurchase lets you get 1i+(10s on attack &amp; damage roll) (max 5)<b> aggravated</b> damage on it.<br /> <br /> This is in many ways superior to The Dragon Dies Screaming (in comparison wasp lunar gets +4 duration, on average equal damage attacking with 10i, and lower penalty) from White Veil but instead of 6m 6i 1WP you just pay 3m 2i and you get to do it with Miniscule Size bonuses and flight. Pretty brutal for a lunar assassin.<br /> <br /> Edit: I remembered Vance has said they are going to explicitly allow enhanced toxin mutations to enhance creatures natural venoms so numbers went up.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: This works at E1 with octopi since they dont need the damage boost and only the duration from the first purchase of Mamba-and-Cobra, but if you want to do it on land you need to be some sort of chimeric flying octopus abomination. Being a wasp is just cleaner, though I wish we had like black-widow stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Octopuses are already capable of moving around on land in real life, they're just at risk of suffocating if they stay out too long. That should mean that they don't treat land as difficult terrain. Shifting Breath Inversion fixes the suffocation issue and has one of the the same prerequisites as the poison set up anyway.<br /> <br /> You can even go for the Tiny Creature octopus so that you can use the great Protean effects in the Dexterity Defense tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T17:33:32-07:00","id":1300425,"title":"","content":"Just saw that Vance said on Discord that Mamba and Cobra only increases One of damage/penalty/duration per 10. Not that it\u2019s a massive dealbreaker, but just wondering if it\u2019s been included in the calculation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T22:46:35-07:00","id":1300473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300425#post1300425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw that Vance said on Discord that Mamba and Cobra only increases One of damage/penalty/duration per 10. Not that it\u2019s a massive dealbreaker, but just wondering if it\u2019s been included in the calculation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is. Base duration 6, up to 8 with enhanced toxin, 8+essence with Adder Fang, 9+essence with base effect of Mamba-and-Cobra (without any 10s rolled), then throw all 10s on the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T22:50:14-07:00","id":1300474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300473#post1300473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is. Base duration 6, up to 8 with enhanced toxin, 8+essence with Adder Fang, 9+essence with base effect of Mamba-and-Cobra (without any 10s rolled), then throw all 10s on the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, excellent. That \u201cCheat yourself one higher Ess Charm\u201d ability of the Glory Sphere is certainly seeing more play than I initially expected. <br /> <br /> If you were building this character from Ess1, which Ess 2 Charm would you pick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 03-28-2019, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T23:04:30-07:00","id":1300475,"title":"","content":"Probably just Claws of the Silver Moon so you can deal some initiative damage. Without it and it prerequisites you basically can't deal initiative damage in Miniscule size.<br /> <br /> It's either that or Last Warriors Unity some moonsilver brawl weapon, because you are never doing more than overwhelming + post soak adders. You are pretty good at killing enemies your buddies crash since you dont really need the initiative for anything but beating hardness.<br /> <br /> It's really leans more toward an assassin build than a real combat monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-28-2019, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T01:13:01-07:00","id":1300493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300404#post1300404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Octopuses are already capable of moving around on land in real life, they're just at risk of suffocating if they stay out too long. That should mean that they don't treat land as difficult terrain. Shifting Breath Inversion fixes the suffocation issue and has one of the the same prerequisites as the poison set up anyway.<br /> <br /> You can even go for the Tiny Creature octopus so that you can use the great Protean effects in the Dexterity Defense tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I didnt see the rules for making a water-based creature fully capable on land hidden away in Shifting Breath Inversion (I was going to just use Gills mutation since at 3 dots it lets you breathe both air and water). So even if I personally feel unsure about allowing an octopus full speed on land without any mutation we just need extra limbs and we can RAW move on land at full speed for sure. That probably makes octopus superior to wasp.<br /> <br /> So lets say chimera of octopus and spider, with extra limbs as our tell, wall walking + enhanced toxin as our Chimera-soul expression, and Breath Inversion. Now we're moving at full speed running on walls. Also as a tiny octopus with Skulking Rat Spirit we roll stealth with double 9s, rerolling 1s and 2s, and -2 successes on enemy rolls to notice us.<br /> <br /> Spidersquid, spidersquid, does whatever a spidersquid does.<br /> <br /> At E1 with Mamba-and-Cobra our poison is doing 4i Aggravated with a 7+(10s on attack and damage roll) duration, which will increase with our essence. Not shabby. We're also crazy stealthy and between wall walking and amorphous body there's hardly anywhere we can't get in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-28-2019, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T01:53:03-07:00","id":1300497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300493#post1300493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So lets say chimera of octopus and spider, with extra limbs as our tell, wall walking + enhanced toxin as our Chimera-soul expression, and Breath Inversion. Now we're moving at full speed running on walls. Also as a tiny octopus with Skulking Rat Spirit we roll stealth with double 9s, rerolling 1s and 2s, and -2 successes on enemy rolls to notice us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Octopus + Cat gives that nice Xenomorph look, especially if you put the Ocotopus' beak at the tip of your tail or as a secondary mouth into your main one. The Octopus' suckers are probably sufficient to get the wall walking mutation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T02:07:56-07:00","id":1300500,"title":"","content":"Problem is we want Enhanced Toxin, and at E1 we have to get it from Chimera Soul Expression to apply it to our octopus form, so whatever animal we chimera the octopus with probably also has to be poisonous.<br /> <br /> I figure the monster ends up looking something like a mouse to rat sized large-headed crab-spider with two big octopus eyes, a beak, and some longer 'arms' around it mouth-parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T02:50:41-07:00","id":1300504,"title":"","content":"That both animals have to be poisonous does limit the number of possible combinations. For an assassin build it would be great to have an animal in there that gives access to flight and enhanced senses as well, especially night vision, for later upgrades to the form.<br /> <br /> Though for double poisonous forms octopus + platypus would be worth it just for how hilariously freaky it would look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T09:51:49-07:00","id":1300573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300500#post1300500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is we want Enhanced Toxin, and at E1 we have to get it from Chimera Soul Expression to apply it to our octopus form, so whatever animal we chimera the octopus with probably also has to be poisonous.<br /> <br /> I figure the monster ends up looking something like a mouse to rat sized large-headed crab-spider with two big octopus eyes, a beak, and some longer 'arms' around it mouth-parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you attach Enhanced Toxin to the Tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:35:50-07:00","id":1300594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300573#post1300573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Couldn't you attach Enhanced Toxin to the Tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you cant take Enhanced Toxin without having some form of natural poison, and if its your Tell you got to have it in all your forms, so I'm not sure its legal to have a Tell mutation with prerequisites you dont have, or if you can tie multiple mutations to the tell for Venomous + Enhanced Toxin (and that would be 3 merit points spend on a useless venomous mutation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:59:40-07:00","id":1301294,"title":"","content":"So pestletails right, they're great, superb tanks. But what if they could be sorcerers and amazing tanks at the same time?<br /> <br /> Enter Extra Limbs mutation, Shadow-Hands Invocation (E2, so need Glory Sphere), and Natural Shield mutation. Combined they let us flurry Shape Sorcery &amp; Full Defense with no penalties. Combine this with pestletails Bony Shell (no initiative lost and +4 soak and hardness on full defense) and Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance (free defend other every turn) we can make ourselves and a buddy extremely hard to damage while casting spells unhindered, at E1, for 2m/round.<br /> <br /> Technically this mutation-charm combination should also work with Crane Style (though obviously you have to drop being a pestletail) even if the natural-shield weapon isn't style compatible, due to how Full Defense is written and that Vance has said:<br /> <br /> &quot;Martial Arts don't care if your full defense benefits from the shield tag, even if they aren't shield-compatible (although note that shields don't let you flurry attacks and full defenses).&quot; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1262380#post1262380\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...80#post1262380</a><br /> <br /> Which seems like it might be even stronger, though obviously you dont get the insane soak/hardness of an all-out-defending pestletail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-31-2019, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:48:26-07:00","id":1301608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms?p=1300224#post1300224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok hear me out: Wasps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think you caught on to something terrifying here, as this is more vicious than Silver Claws although your flat unable to do decisive damage normally.<br /> Without even using the Mamba and Cobra Mastery, this is terrifying for a hit &amp; run character. Although the low armor can be a problem perhaps using stealth for hit and run Ninja style is the optimal for this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal form only stuff...</b><br /> <i><b>Wasp</b></i><br /> <b>Defense Values: </b>9 evasion (18 dice for a 50% chance to hit or needing 20 if they are poisoned?)<br /> <b>Soak:</b> 1, 0 hardness (I think Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze are likely a better purchase than Mamba &amp; Cobra Mastery here. it also lets you take the name Silver Wasp)<br /> <b>Stealth: </b>-3 successes to see it, so an average of 18 dice would fail to find you after a sting.<br /> <b>Attack: </b>Sting 13 dice attack<br /> Poison with damage 1i/round (B in Crash), duration 6 rounds, and a \u22122 penalty.<br /> Stamina 5, and +5 points of mutations beyond the venomous mutation: 5 uses, Duration 8 with a minimum of 1 round<br /> <br /> <b>Adder Fang Method:</b><br /> If you run out of the poison it costs you 3 motes per poison attempt and extends it to 9 rounds at Essence 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence 2: Mamba &amp; Cobra Mastery vs. Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace</b><br /> IMC: Lose 1 evasion defense value to get 11 soak &amp; 10 hardness...<br /> M&amp;CM: 10 rounds per hit, +10's on attack or damage extend duration, &amp; now does Aggravated Damage...<br /> -Averages make this 12 poison difficulty with a minimum of 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T12:29:45-07:00","id":1308367,"title":"","content":"I've been looking into Lunar grapplers a bit, and honestly they seem absolutely terrifying once they aquire Jaws of the River Dragon.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm missing something there's nothing stopping you from stacking Finding the Needles Eye + Hunter's Eye Precision + Jaws of the River Dragon on a Grapple attack, which with a one-point stunt, Dex 5, Str 5, Brawl 5 and a speciality would let you roll the attack with 26 dice, reroll 1s and double 9s, for an average 17.16 successes, ignoring 1 point of defense bonus from Medium weapon etc.<br /> <br /> Even a high-essence Dawn melee supernal is going to wish he branched out and got Seven-Shadows Evasion, and you can do it out to medium range with Kraken-Arm Lash.<br /> <br /> So now we just have to find the most OP grappling animal. Legendary Size creatures have the gigantic advantage of making unopposed control rolls against anyone who isn't a serious superpowered grappler themselves, but Mountainous Spirit Expression is a charm and at least two non-legendary size animals have abilities that to me make them quite interesting.<br /> <br /> (Bears, Great Cats, and a few other animals have a cool ability for initiating a grapple from a withering attack, but since Jaws of the River Dragon and Kraken-Arm Lash require you to actually use a grapple attack that isn't very synergistic so I'm not listing them.)<br /> <br /> Death Moa can grapple from short range without a charm which is quite neat.<br /> <br /> Tyrant Lizards have Deadly Trash, letting them savage before throwing without reseting between and then they get bonus initiative after reset for how many turns of control they gave up, don't take defense penalties for grappling non-legendary size enemies, can drag reflexively, and only lose rounds of control when damaged. I don't think I need to tell anyone these things are terrifying. For straight-up brawlers not intersted in doing anything sneaky or fancy that just want to do maximum damage, this seems the way to go.<br /> <br /> River Dragons have Death Roll, which confuses me because what is the point of having double 7s on savaging decisive attacks when those are usually unrolled. If its supposed to mean double 7s on the damage roll then holy crap, that hurts.<br /> <br /> Edit: Vance confirmed the Death Roll is double 7s on damage. Spine-Breaking Technique with Death Roll seems really brutal, rolling a decisive savaging attack with double 7s on damage without resetting. You could even do that, then turn into a Tyrant Lizard and savage + throw, rolling 3 decisive attacks over 3 turns (2 turns with Behemoth-and-Flea Mastery at E5) before resetting, the first one of them with double 7s on damage. And at the end of it when they die tyrant lizard merits give you back 1 WP and initiative equal to the number of rounds of control left.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: So in animal forms with a crippling attack, like River Dragons, inflicting a crippling injury gives you back the WP spend on Limb-Maiming Flourish. But Death Roll always inflicts a crippling injury. So you get to roll all dice that showed successes again for just 3m, at which point you are averaging more successes on the damage roll than the number of dice you are rolling.<br /> <br /> Strix can move normally while grappling as long as they're in flight, which combined with Kraken-Arm Lash to pick people up from two range bands above makes them perfect for hit-and-run tactics. Combined with its Night Vision, Eagle Eye, and the stealth abilities of lunars, an attack from a strix form lunar at night would be fucking terrifying. Talons reach down impossibly from a silent shadow moving swiftly across the night sky, stealing immaculates away into the darkness one by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-28-2019, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}